1
00:01:21,677 --> 00:01:26,671
I should've known that you would
be here, Professor McGonagall.

2
00:01:37,901 --> 00:01:41,068
Good evening, Professor Dumbledore.

3
00:01:43,573 --> 00:01:46,574
Are the rumors true, Albus?

4
00:01:46,827 --> 00:01:52,034
I'm afraid so, professor.
The good and the bad.

5
00:01:52,248 --> 00:01:55,499
- And the boy?
- Hagrid is bringing him.

6
00:01:55,752 --> 00:01:59,665
Is it wise to trust Hagrid
with something so important?

7
00:02:00,172 --> 00:02:05,084
Professor, I would trust Hagrid
with my life.

8
00:02:23,947 --> 00:02:28,075
Professor Dumbledore, sir.
Professor McGonagall.

9
00:02:28,285 --> 00:02:32,152
- No problems, I trust, Hagrid?
- No, sir.

10
00:02:32,372 --> 00:02:36,832
Little tyke fell asleep
as we were flying over Bristol.

11
00:02:37,626 --> 00:02:40,118
Try not to wake him.

12
00:02:40,921 --> 00:02:42,998
There you go.

13
00:02:48,429 --> 00:02:52,972
Do you really think it's safe,
leaving him with these people?

14
00:02:53,184 --> 00:02:58,427
I've watched them all day.
They're the worst sort of Muggles.

15
00:02:58,689 --> 00:03:02,639
- They really are...
- The only family he has.

16
00:03:02,902 --> 00:03:07,813
He'll be famous. Every child
in our world will know his name.

17
00:03:08,073 --> 00:03:09,781
Exactly.

18
00:03:09,991 --> 00:03:14,285
He's far better off growing up
away from all of that.

19
00:03:16,749 --> 00:03:19,500
Until he's ready.

20
00:03:31,514 --> 00:03:37,017
There, there, Hagrid.
It's not really goodbye, after all.

21
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:50,358
Good luck...

22
00:03:51,033 --> 00:03:53,523
...Harry Potter.

23
00:04:11,094 --> 00:04:14,095
Up. Get up!

24
00:04:16,725 --> 00:04:18,219
Now!

25
00:04:31,905 --> 00:04:35,275
Wake up, cousin!
We're going to the zoo!

26
00:04:46,462 --> 00:04:51,753
- Here he comes, the birthday boy.
- Happy birthday, son.

27
00:04:53,594 --> 00:04:56,760
Cook breakfast.
And try not to burn anything.

28
00:04:56,972 --> 00:05:01,929
- Yes, Aunt Petunia.
- I want everything to be perfect...

29
00:05:02,143 --> 00:05:05,061
...for my Dudley's special day!

30
00:05:05,271 --> 00:05:10,265
- Hurry up! Bring my coffee, boy.
- Yes, Uncle Vernon.

31
00:05:11,486 --> 00:05:14,606
Aren't they wonderful, darling?

32
00:05:16,784 --> 00:05:20,283
- How many are there?
- 36. Counted them myself.

33
00:05:20,496 --> 00:05:23,699
36?! But last year I had 37!

34
00:05:23,916 --> 00:05:27,783
- But some are bigger than last year's.
- I don't care!

35
00:05:28,004 --> 00:05:30,494
This is what we're going to do.

36
00:05:30,714 --> 00:05:35,091
We're going to buy you two
new presents. How's that, pumpkin?

37
00:05:37,053 --> 00:05:42,676
It should be a lovely day at the zoo.
I'm really looking forward to it.

38
00:05:45,979 --> 00:05:47,805
I'm warning you now, boy.

39
00:05:48,022 --> 00:05:51,521
Any funny business, any at all...

40
00:05:51,734 --> 00:05:54,770
...and you won't have
any meals for a week.

41
00:05:55,531 --> 00:05:57,273
Get in.

42
00:06:04,456 --> 00:06:06,862
Make it move.

43
00:06:09,543 --> 00:06:11,251
Move!

44
00:06:11,504 --> 00:06:13,959
- Move!
- He's asleep!

45
00:06:14,173 --> 00:06:16,711
He's boring.

46
00:06:19,136 --> 00:06:20,595
Sorry about him.

47
00:06:20,804 --> 00:06:24,504
He doesn't understand
what it's like, lying there...

48
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:28,884
...watching people press
their ugly faces in on you.

49
00:06:31,649 --> 00:06:34,318
Can you hear me?

50
00:06:36,821 --> 00:06:40,865
It's just, I've never talked
to a snake before.

51
00:06:41,325 --> 00:06:42,736
Do you?

52
00:06:42,952 --> 00:06:47,080
Do you talk to people often?

53
00:06:48,207 --> 00:06:51,492
You're from Burma, aren't you?
Was it nice there?

54
00:06:51,710 --> 00:06:53,999
Do you miss your family?

55
00:06:56,882 --> 00:07:01,590
I see. That's me as well.
I never knew my parents either.

56
00:07:01,803 --> 00:07:06,797
Mummy, Dad, you won't believe
what this snake is doing!

57
00:07:29,914 --> 00:07:31,907
Thanks.

58
00:07:32,124 --> 00:07:33,536
Anytime.

59
00:07:36,879 --> 00:07:38,788
Snake!

60
00:07:54,271 --> 00:07:57,605
Mum! Mummy! Help me!

61
00:07:57,858 --> 00:08:00,978
My darling boy!
How did you get in there?

62
00:08:01,487 --> 00:08:06,563
Who did this? How did you get
in there? Is there a snake?

63
00:08:11,455 --> 00:08:16,746
It's all right, sweetheart.
We'll get you out of these cold clothes.

64
00:08:18,504 --> 00:08:21,422
- What happened?
- I swear, I don't know!

65
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:25,499
The glass was there
and then it was gone, like magic.

66
00:08:29,932 --> 00:08:32,719
There's no such thing as magic.

67
00:09:09,512 --> 00:09:12,181
Marge is ill. Ate a funny whelk.

68
00:09:12,389 --> 00:09:15,593
- Dad, look! Harry's got a letter!
- It's mine!

69
00:09:15,810 --> 00:09:18,561
Yours? Who'd be writing to you?

70
00:09:49,844 --> 00:09:54,387
No more mail through this letterbox.

71
00:10:06,568 --> 00:10:09,403
Have a lovely day at the office, dear.

72
00:10:12,283 --> 00:10:14,952
Shoo! Go on.

73
00:10:39,809 --> 00:10:42,679
Fine day, Sunday.

74
00:10:43,313 --> 00:10:47,975
In my opinion, best day of the week.
Why is that, Dudley?

75
00:10:48,193 --> 00:10:52,606
- Because there's no post on Sundays?
- Right you are, Harry!

76
00:10:52,822 --> 00:10:55,573
No post on Sunday.

77
00:10:56,993 --> 00:11:00,907
No blasted letters today! No, sir.

78
00:11:01,497 --> 00:11:06,455
Not one single bloody letter. Not one!

79
00:11:14,885 --> 00:11:18,752
No, sir, not one blasted, miserable...

80
00:11:30,276 --> 00:11:32,482
Make it stop, please!

81
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:36,189
Stop it!

82
00:11:40,328 --> 00:11:43,282
Mummy, what's happening?

83
00:11:46,709 --> 00:11:51,038
Give me that! Give me that letter!

84
00:11:53,673 --> 00:11:55,417
Get off!

85
00:11:59,179 --> 00:12:03,343
They're my letters! Let go of me!

86
00:12:04,184 --> 00:12:07,185
That's it! We're going away!

87
00:12:07,855 --> 00:12:11,520
Far away, where they can't find us!

88
00:12:11,733 --> 00:12:14,983
Daddy's gone mad, hasn't he?

89
00:12:49,896 --> 00:12:52,185
Make a wish, Harry.

90
00:13:08,290 --> 00:13:10,329
Who's there?

91
00:13:22,512 --> 00:13:24,919
Sorry about that.

92
00:13:31,812 --> 00:13:36,389
I demand that you leave at once.
You are breaking and entering.

93
00:13:39,277 --> 00:13:42,112
Dry up, Dursley, you great prune.

94
00:13:47,327 --> 00:13:50,826
I haven't seen you
since you was a baby, Harry.

95
00:13:51,039 --> 00:13:55,582
You're a bit more along than I expected.
Particularly in the middle.

96
00:13:55,794 --> 00:13:58,629
I'm not Harry.

97
00:14:00,465 --> 00:14:04,165
- I am.
- Well, of course you are.

98
00:14:04,968 --> 00:14:06,546
Got something for you.

99
00:14:06,762 --> 00:14:12,348
Afraid I sat on it, but I imagine
it'll taste fine just the same.

100
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:18,270
Baked it myself, words and all.

101
00:14:23,822 --> 00:14:24,853
Thank you.

102
00:14:25,115 --> 00:14:29,243
It's not every day your young man
turns 11, is it?

103
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:48,553
Excuse me, but who are you?

104
00:14:48,762 --> 00:14:53,673
Rubeus Hagrid, Keeper of Keys
and Grounds at Hogwarts.

105
00:14:53,934 --> 00:14:57,635
- Of course, you know about Hogwarts.
- Sorry, no.

106
00:14:58,231 --> 00:15:03,141
Didn't you ever wonder where
your mum and dad learned it all?

107
00:15:03,403 --> 00:15:04,778
Learned what?

108
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:07,525
You're a wizard, Harry.

109
00:15:08,740 --> 00:15:10,780
- I'm a what?
- A wizard.

110
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:14,029
A good one, I'd wager,
once you're trained up.

111
00:15:14,287 --> 00:15:17,158
No, you've made a mistake.
I mean...

112
00:15:17,374 --> 00:15:20,375
...I can't be a wizard.

113
00:15:21,044 --> 00:15:25,789
I mean, I'm just Harry. Just Harry.

114
00:15:26,882 --> 00:15:30,880
Well, Just Harry, did you ever
make anything happen?

115
00:15:31,095 --> 00:15:35,757
Anything you couldn't explain,
when you were angry or scared?

116
00:15:52,159 --> 00:15:55,278
"Dear Mr. Potter,
We are pleased to accept you...

117
00:15:55,495 --> 00:15:58,745
...at Hogwarts School
of Witchcraft and Wizardry."

118
00:15:58,957 --> 00:16:03,914
He will not be going! We swore
we'd put a stop to all this rubbish.

119
00:16:04,128 --> 00:16:08,339
You knew? You knew all along
and you never told me?

120
00:16:08,549 --> 00:16:11,633
Of course we knew.
How could you not be?

121
00:16:11,845 --> 00:16:15,546
My perfect sister being who she was.

122
00:16:15,766 --> 00:16:21,719
My mother and father were so proud
the day she got her letter.

123
00:16:21,937 --> 00:16:26,101
"We have a witch in the family.
Isn't it wonderful?"

124
00:16:26,317 --> 00:16:29,982
I was the only one to see her
for what she was.

125
00:16:30,196 --> 00:16:31,939
A freak!

126
00:16:32,155 --> 00:16:35,109
Then she met that Potter,
and then she had you...

127
00:16:35,325 --> 00:16:41,030
...and I knew you would be the same.
Just as strange, just as abnormal.

128
00:16:41,248 --> 00:16:46,242
And then she got herself blown up,
and we got landed with you.

129
00:16:46,462 --> 00:16:50,460
Blown up? You told me
my parents died in a car crash.

130
00:16:50,716 --> 00:16:55,010
A car crash? A car crash killed
Lily and James Potter?

131
00:16:55,220 --> 00:16:59,134
- We had to say something.
- It's an outrage! A scandal!

132
00:16:59,349 --> 00:17:01,804
He'll not be going.

133
00:17:02,018 --> 00:17:05,351
A great Muggle like you
is going to stop him?

134
00:17:05,521 --> 00:17:06,553
Muggle?

135
00:17:06,898 --> 00:17:10,895
Non-magic folk. This boy's had
his name down since he were born.

136
00:17:11,110 --> 00:17:14,978
He's going to the finest school
of witchcraft and wizardry.

137
00:17:15,199 --> 00:17:21,117
He'll be under the finest headmaster
Hogwarts has seen, Albus Dumbledore.

138
00:17:21,330 --> 00:17:26,122
I will not pay to have a crackpot
old fool teach him magic tricks.

139
00:17:26,335 --> 00:17:30,877
Never insult Albus Dumbledore...

140
00:17:31,089 --> 00:17:33,129
...in front of me.

141
00:17:51,025 --> 00:17:56,268
I'd appreciate it if you didn't tell
anyone at Hogwarts about that.

142
00:17:56,530 --> 00:18:00,611
- I'm not allowed to do magic.
- Okay.

143
00:18:01,911 --> 00:18:04,912
We're a bit behind schedule.
Best be off.

144
00:18:11,087 --> 00:18:14,290
Unless you'd rather stay, of course.

145
00:18:28,603 --> 00:18:31,889
"All students must be equipped with...

146
00:18:32,106 --> 00:18:35,023
...one standard size 2
pewter cauldron...

147
00:18:35,236 --> 00:18:41,024
...and may bring, if they desire,
either an owl, a cat or a toad."

148
00:18:41,283 --> 00:18:43,856
Can we find all this in London?

149
00:18:44,078 --> 00:18:46,451
If you know where to go.

150
00:19:09,227 --> 00:19:12,181
Ah, Hagrid! The usual, I presume?

151
00:19:12,397 --> 00:19:16,264
No, thanks, Tom.
I'm on official Hogwarts business.

152
00:19:16,484 --> 00:19:19,569
Just helping Harry buy
his school supplies.

153
00:19:19,821 --> 00:19:23,356
Bless my soul.
It's Harry Potter!

154
00:19:27,662 --> 00:19:31,113
Welcome back, Mr. Potter.
Welcome back.

155
00:19:31,332 --> 00:19:35,661
Doris Crockford. I can't believe
I'm meeting you at last.

156
00:19:36,128 --> 00:19:41,371
Harry Potter. Can't tell you
how pleased I am to meet you.

157
00:19:41,592 --> 00:19:44,129
Hello, professor. I didn't see you.

158
00:19:44,344 --> 00:19:49,338
Professor Quirrell will be your
Defense Against the Dark Arts teacher.

159
00:19:49,558 --> 00:19:51,966
Oh, nice to meet you.

160
00:19:52,227 --> 00:19:55,312
Fearfully fascinating subject.

161
00:19:55,523 --> 00:20:00,149
Not that you need it, eh, Potter?

162
00:20:01,069 --> 00:20:05,233
Yes, well, must be going now.
Lots to buy.

163
00:20:05,449 --> 00:20:07,192
Goodbye.

164
00:20:09,912 --> 00:20:13,494
- See, Harry? You're famous.
- But why am I famous?

165
00:20:13,707 --> 00:20:17,159
All those people,
how is it they know who I am?

166
00:20:17,377 --> 00:20:21,161
I'm not sure I'm the right person
to tell you that.

167
00:20:38,190 --> 00:20:41,939
Welcome, Harry, to Diagon Alley.

168
00:20:58,292 --> 00:21:00,783
Here, you get your quills and ink.

169
00:21:01,046 --> 00:21:04,960
Over there, all your bits and bobs
for doing wizardry.

170
00:21:29,823 --> 00:21:32,064
It's a world-class racing broom.

171
00:21:32,283 --> 00:21:36,151
Look at it! The new Nimbus 2000!

172
00:21:36,414 --> 00:21:39,699
It's the fastest model yet.

173
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:47,998
But how am I to pay for all this?
I haven't any money.

174
00:21:48,217 --> 00:21:51,587
There's your money.
Gringotts, the wizard bank.

175
00:21:51,804 --> 00:21:57,309
Ain't no safer place, not one.
Except perhaps Hogwarts.

176
00:22:09,946 --> 00:22:13,944
Hagrid, what exactly
are these things?

177
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:19,402
They're goblins. Clever as they come,
but not the most friendly of beasts.

178
00:22:19,623 --> 00:22:21,580
Best stay close.

179
00:22:25,629 --> 00:22:29,293
Mr. Harry Potter wishes
to make a withdrawal.

180
00:22:33,511 --> 00:22:36,678
And does Mr. Harry Potter
have his key?

181
00:22:37,640 --> 00:22:40,843
Wait a minute.
Got it here somewhere.

182
00:22:43,688 --> 00:22:46,523
Ha! There's the little devil.

183
00:22:46,732 --> 00:22:49,602
And there's something else as well.

184
00:22:50,862 --> 00:22:54,196
Professor Dumbledore gave me this.

185
00:22:58,244 --> 00:23:03,321
It's about You-Know-What
in vault you-know-which.

186
00:23:04,625 --> 00:23:06,582
Very well.

187
00:23:11,798 --> 00:23:14,633
Vault 687.

188
00:23:16,554 --> 00:23:18,842
Lamp, please.

189
00:23:27,357 --> 00:23:28,685
Key, please.

190
00:23:52,131 --> 00:23:55,878
Did you think your parents
would leave you with nothing?

191
00:23:57,177 --> 00:24:00,877
- Vault 713.
- What's in there, Hagrid?

192
00:24:01,098 --> 00:24:05,261
Can't tell you.
Hogwarts business. Very secret.

193
00:24:05,518 --> 00:24:07,061
Stand back.

194
00:24:35,339 --> 00:24:38,126
Best not to mention this to anyone.

195
00:24:46,560 --> 00:24:50,473
I still need a wand.

196
00:24:50,688 --> 00:24:54,104
You want Ollivanders.
There ain't no place better.

197
00:24:54,817 --> 00:24:59,942
Run along there and wait.
I got one more thing to do.

198
00:25:17,924 --> 00:25:19,751
Hello?

199
00:25:22,719 --> 00:25:24,546
Hello?

200
00:25:28,058 --> 00:25:32,352
I wondered when
I'd be seeing you, Mr. Potter.

201
00:25:40,153 --> 00:25:42,359
It seems only yesterday...

202
00:25:42,614 --> 00:25:48,450
...that your mother and father were
in here buying their first wands.

203
00:25:55,126 --> 00:25:57,415
Here we are.

204
00:26:06,011 --> 00:26:08,549
Give it a wave.

205
00:26:15,020 --> 00:26:17,558
Apparently not.

206
00:26:24,990 --> 00:26:27,197
Perhaps...

207
00:26:28,868 --> 00:26:31,026
...this.

208
00:26:38,085 --> 00:26:42,712
No, no, definitely not.
No matter.

209
00:26:49,930 --> 00:26:51,555
I wonder...

210
00:27:20,751 --> 00:27:23,040
Curious.

211
00:27:23,254 --> 00:27:26,172
Very curious.

212
00:27:26,382 --> 00:27:29,502
Sorry, but what's curious?

213
00:27:31,220 --> 00:27:34,506
I remember every wand
I've ever sold, Mr. Potter.

214
00:27:34,724 --> 00:27:37,475
It so happens that the phoenix...

215
00:27:37,685 --> 00:27:42,395
...whose tail feather resides
in your wand, gave another feather.

216
00:27:42,816 --> 00:27:45,899
Just one other.

217
00:27:46,112 --> 00:27:50,441
It is curious that you should
be destined for this wand...

218
00:27:50,699 --> 00:27:56,369
...when its brother
gave you that scar.

219
00:27:58,206 --> 00:28:01,409
And who owned that wand?

220
00:28:02,252 --> 00:28:04,659
We do not speak his name.

221
00:28:05,129 --> 00:28:08,629
The wand chooses
the wizard, Mr. Potter.

222
00:28:08,841 --> 00:28:11,842
It's not always clear why.

223
00:28:12,219 --> 00:28:15,718
But I think it is clear...

224
00:28:15,932 --> 00:28:19,847
...that we can expect
great things from you.

225
00:28:20,061 --> 00:28:24,307
After all, He-Who-Must-Not-Be-Named...

226
00:28:24,566 --> 00:28:27,235
...did great things.

227
00:28:27,443 --> 00:28:29,436
Terrible...

228
00:28:29,903 --> 00:28:33,154
...yes, but great.

229
00:28:38,787 --> 00:28:40,827
Harry! Harry!

230
00:28:41,206 --> 00:28:43,578
Happy birthday.

231
00:28:50,716 --> 00:28:54,215
You all right, Harry?
You seem very quiet.

232
00:28:54,595 --> 00:29:00,181
He killed my parents, didn't he?
The one who gave me this.

233
00:29:00,392 --> 00:29:04,010
You know, Hagrid. I know you do.

234
00:29:07,899 --> 00:29:12,442
First, and understand this
because it's very important:

235
00:29:12,653 --> 00:29:15,191
Not all wizards are good.

236
00:29:15,406 --> 00:29:17,897
Some of them go bad.
A few years ago...

237
00:29:18,118 --> 00:29:23,112
...there was a wizard who went as bad
as you can go. His name was V...

238
00:29:23,331 --> 00:29:26,950
- His name was V...
- Maybe if you wrote it down?

239
00:29:27,170 --> 00:29:29,043
No, I can't spell it.

240
00:29:29,254 --> 00:29:33,502
- All right, Voldemort.
- Voldemort?

241
00:29:37,471 --> 00:29:39,713
It was dark times, Harry.

242
00:29:42,016 --> 00:29:45,136
<i>Voldemort started
to gather some followers.</i>

243
00:29:45,394 --> 00:29:48,728
<i>Brought them over to the Dark Side.</i>

244
00:29:50,107 --> 00:29:53,227
<i>Anyone that stood up to him
ended up dead.</i>

245
00:29:54,362 --> 00:29:57,398
<i>Your parents fought against him.</i>

246
00:29:57,615 --> 00:30:01,399
<i>But nobody lived once
he decided to kill them.</i>

247
00:30:05,790 --> 00:30:08,363
<i>Nobody, not one.</i>

248
00:30:08,584 --> 00:30:10,957
<i>Except you.</i>

249
00:30:12,963 --> 00:30:17,091
Me? Voldemort tried to kill me?

250
00:30:17,551 --> 00:30:21,715
Yes. That ain't no ordinary cut
on your forehead, Harry.

251
00:30:22,013 --> 00:30:27,767
A mark like that only comes from being
touched by a curse, an evil curse.

252
00:30:27,978 --> 00:30:31,596
What happened to V?
To You-Know-Who?

253
00:30:32,732 --> 00:30:36,101
Well, some say he died.

254
00:30:36,319 --> 00:30:38,726
Codswallop, in my opinion.

255
00:30:38,947 --> 00:30:42,198
Nope, I reckon he's out there still...

256
00:30:42,409 --> 00:30:45,363
...too tired to carry on.

257
00:30:45,579 --> 00:30:50,999
But one thing's certain. Something
about you stumped him that night.

258
00:30:51,252 --> 00:30:55,498
That's why you're famous.
That's why everybody knows your name.

259
00:30:55,965 --> 00:30:59,630
You're the boy who lived.

260
00:31:08,976 --> 00:31:11,681
What are you looking at?

261
00:31:13,439 --> 00:31:15,432
Blimey, is that the time?

262
00:31:15,651 --> 00:31:19,648
I'm gonna have to leave you.
Dumbledore will be wanting his...

263
00:31:19,863 --> 00:31:24,738
Well, he'll be wanting to see me.
Your train leaves in 10 minutes.

264
00:31:24,951 --> 00:31:30,289
Here's your ticket. Stick to your ticket,
that's very important.

265
00:31:33,167 --> 00:31:35,409
"Platform 93/4"?

266
00:31:35,628 --> 00:31:40,420
But, Hagrid, there must be a mistake.
This says platform 93/4.

267
00:31:40,633 --> 00:31:43,966
There's no such thing, is there?

268
00:32:02,488 --> 00:32:04,066
Sorry.

269
00:32:05,573 --> 00:32:08,326
Excuse me. Excuse me.

270
00:32:08,535 --> 00:32:10,077
On your left.

271
00:32:10,329 --> 00:32:14,113
Can you tell me where
I might find platform 93/4?

272
00:32:14,333 --> 00:32:16,870
Think you're being funny, do you?

273
00:32:17,085 --> 00:32:20,418
It's the same every year,
packed with Muggles.

274
00:32:20,881 --> 00:32:24,250
- Muggles?
- Platform 93/4, this way.

275
00:32:29,932 --> 00:32:33,098
All right, Percy, you first.

276
00:32:43,070 --> 00:32:44,267
Fred, you next.

277
00:32:44,487 --> 00:32:48,188
- He's not Fred, I am.
- You call yourself our mother?

278
00:32:48,408 --> 00:32:50,365
I'm sorry, George.

279
00:32:54,497 --> 00:32:56,904
I'm only joking. I am Fred.

280
00:33:02,714 --> 00:33:05,287
Excuse me.

281
00:33:06,385 --> 00:33:09,171
Could you tell me how to?

282
00:33:09,388 --> 00:33:12,922
How to get onto the platform?
Not to worry, dear.

283
00:33:13,141 --> 00:33:15,596
It's Ron's first time
to Hogwarts as well.

284
00:33:15,810 --> 00:33:21,729
All you do is walk straight at the wall
between platforms 9 and 10.

285
00:33:21,940 --> 00:33:25,392
- Best to run if you're nervous.
- Good luck.

286
00:34:23,001 --> 00:34:27,249
Excuse me. Do you mind?
Everywhere else is full.

287
00:34:27,464 --> 00:34:29,670
Not at all.

288
00:34:32,760 --> 00:34:35,168
I'm Ron, by the way.
Ron Weasley.

289
00:34:35,430 --> 00:34:38,051
I'm Harry. Harry Potter.

290
00:34:39,434 --> 00:34:41,473
So it's true!

291
00:34:41,685 --> 00:34:44,472
I mean, do you really have the?

292
00:34:45,064 --> 00:34:47,934
- The what?
- The scar?

293
00:34:51,112 --> 00:34:53,318
Wicked!

294
00:34:55,783 --> 00:35:00,943
- Anything off the trolley, dears?
- No, thanks. I'm all set.

295
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:07,289
We'll take the lot.

296
00:35:18,013 --> 00:35:22,805
- Bertie Bott's Every Flavor Beans?
- They mean every flavor.

297
00:35:23,227 --> 00:35:26,596
There's chocolate
and peppermint and also...

298
00:35:26,813 --> 00:35:30,645
...spinach, liver and tripe.

299
00:35:30,860 --> 00:35:35,023
George sweared he got
a booger-flavored one once.

300
00:35:39,702 --> 00:35:45,040
- Are they real frogs?
- It's a spell. You want the cards.

301
00:35:45,249 --> 00:35:50,705
Each pack's got a famous witch
or wizard. I've got about 500 meself.

302
00:35:52,214 --> 00:35:54,502
Watch it!

303
00:35:56,509 --> 00:36:00,293
That's rotten luck. They've only
got one good jump in them.

304
00:36:03,182 --> 00:36:07,096
- I've got Dumbledore!
- I got about six of him.

305
00:36:08,856 --> 00:36:10,397
Hey, he's gone!

306
00:36:10,607 --> 00:36:14,058
You can't expect him to
hang around all day, can you?

307
00:36:14,695 --> 00:36:17,813
This is Scabbers.
Pathetic, isn't he?

308
00:36:18,030 --> 00:36:19,193
A little.

309
00:36:19,407 --> 00:36:22,741
Fred gave me a spell
to turn him yellow. Want to see?

310
00:36:22,952 --> 00:36:24,991
Yeah.

311
00:36:31,752 --> 00:36:33,377
Has anyone seen a toad?

312
00:36:33,754 --> 00:36:36,423
- A boy named Neville's lost one.
- No.

313
00:36:37,008 --> 00:36:41,336
Oh, are you doing magic?
Let's see, then.

314
00:36:42,389 --> 00:36:46,718
<i>Sunshine, daisies, butter mellow</i>

315
00:36:46,976 --> 00:36:50,060
<i>Turn this stupid, fat rat yellow</i>

316
00:36:52,816 --> 00:36:58,438
Are you sure that's a real spell?
Well, it's not very good, is it?

317
00:36:58,654 --> 00:37:01,905
I've only tried
a few simple ones myself...

318
00:37:02,116 --> 00:37:04,737
...but they've all worked for me.

319
00:37:08,372 --> 00:37:10,412
For example:

320
00:37:10,791 --> 00:37:13,578
<i>Oculus Reparo.</i>

321
00:37:15,671 --> 00:37:18,292
That's better, isn't it?

322
00:37:19,466 --> 00:37:23,381
Holy cricket, you're Harry Potter!

323
00:37:23,596 --> 00:37:27,178
I'm Hermione Granger.
And you are?

324
00:37:27,892 --> 00:37:31,095
- I'm Ron Weasley.
- Pleasure.

325
00:37:31,311 --> 00:37:36,388
You two better change into robes.
I expect we'll be arriving soon.

326
00:37:40,528 --> 00:37:43,980
You've got dirt on your nose.
Did you know?

327
00:37:44,199 --> 00:37:46,156
Just there.

328
00:37:58,505 --> 00:38:02,289
Right, then.
First years, this way, please!

329
00:38:02,509 --> 00:38:07,715
Come on, first years, don't be shy.
Come on now, hurry up.

330
00:38:14,729 --> 00:38:17,682
- Hello, Harry.
- Hi, Hagrid.

331
00:38:18,774 --> 00:38:23,103
Right, then. This way to the boats.
Come on now, follow me.

332
00:39:08,824 --> 00:39:10,616
Wicked.

333
00:39:38,769 --> 00:39:41,011
Welcome to Hogwarts.

334
00:39:41,231 --> 00:39:45,228
Shortly, you'll pass through
these doors and join your classmates.

335
00:39:45,443 --> 00:39:50,484
But before you take your seats,
you must be sorted into your houses.

336
00:39:50,699 --> 00:39:53,818
They are Gryffindor, Hufflepuff...

337
00:39:54,035 --> 00:39:58,496
...Ravenclaw and Slytherin.

338
00:39:58,915 --> 00:40:03,957
While you're here, your house
will be like your family.

339
00:40:04,587 --> 00:40:08,086
Your triumphs will earn you points.

340
00:40:08,299 --> 00:40:12,427
Any rule-breaking
and you will lose points.

341
00:40:12,636 --> 00:40:17,927
At the end of the year, the house
with the most points wins the house cup.

342
00:40:18,184 --> 00:40:19,465
Trevor!

343
00:40:28,402 --> 00:40:30,027
Sorry.

344
00:40:30,237 --> 00:40:34,187
The Sorting Ceremony
will begin momentarily.

345
00:40:35,535 --> 00:40:38,868
It's true then,
what they're saying on the train.

346
00:40:39,288 --> 00:40:41,909
Harry Potter has come to Hogwarts.

347
00:40:42,124 --> 00:40:43,534
Harry Potter?

348
00:40:44,167 --> 00:40:46,837
This is Crabbe and Goyle.

349
00:40:47,045 --> 00:40:49,334
And I'm Malfoy.

350
00:40:49,673 --> 00:40:51,998
Draco Malfoy.

351
00:40:53,969 --> 00:40:57,552
Think my name's funny, do you?
I've no need to ask yours.

352
00:40:57,764 --> 00:41:03,554
Red hair and a hand-me-down robe?
You must be a Weasley.

353
00:41:04,479 --> 00:41:08,523
You'll find out some wizarding families
are better than others.

354
00:41:08,733 --> 00:41:12,517
You don't want to go making friends
with the wrong sort.

355
00:41:12,737 --> 00:41:14,895
I can help you there.

356
00:41:17,116 --> 00:41:20,948
I think I can tell the wrong sort
for myself, thanks.

357
00:41:26,585 --> 00:41:28,791
We're ready for you now.
Follow me.

358
00:41:47,397 --> 00:41:51,893
The ceiling isn't real. It's bewitched
to look like the night sky.

359
00:41:52,235 --> 00:41:55,105
<i>I read about it
in Hogwarts, A History.</i>

360
00:42:08,376 --> 00:42:11,211
Will you wait along here, please?

361
00:42:12,630 --> 00:42:15,417
Now, before we begin...

362
00:42:15,633 --> 00:42:18,882
...Professor Dumbledore would like
to say a few words.

363
00:42:19,095 --> 00:42:23,886
I have a few start-of-term notices
I wish to announce.

364
00:42:24,265 --> 00:42:26,389
The first years, please note...

365
00:42:26,685 --> 00:42:32,688
...that the Dark Forest is
strictly forbidden to all students.

366
00:42:32,941 --> 00:42:38,445
Also, our caretaker, Mr. Filch,
has asked me to remind you...

367
00:42:38,654 --> 00:42:43,281
...that the third-floor corridor
is out of bounds...

368
00:42:43,576 --> 00:42:47,789
...to everyone who does not wish
to die a most painful death.

369
00:42:49,166 --> 00:42:51,122
Thank you.

370
00:42:52,878 --> 00:42:56,958
When I call your name,
you will come forth.

371
00:42:57,173 --> 00:43:00,792
I shall place the Sorting Hat
on your head...

372
00:43:01,011 --> 00:43:04,214
...and you will be sorted
into your houses.

373
00:43:04,431 --> 00:43:07,052
Hermione Granger.

374
00:43:09,311 --> 00:43:11,931
Oh, no. Okay, relax.

375
00:43:12,314 --> 00:43:15,682
Mental, that one, I'm telling you.

376
00:43:21,156 --> 00:43:25,024
Right, then. Right.

377
00:43:25,243 --> 00:43:28,826
Okay. Gryffindor!

378
00:43:37,629 --> 00:43:40,417
Draco Malfoy.

379
00:43:44,970 --> 00:43:47,176
Slytherin!

380
00:43:48,140 --> 00:43:51,057
Every wizard who went bad
was in Slytherin.

381
00:43:51,268 --> 00:43:53,806
Susan Bones.

382
00:44:02,363 --> 00:44:04,486
Harry, what is it?

383
00:44:04,740 --> 00:44:07,444
Nothing. Nothing, I'm fine.

384
00:44:07,701 --> 00:44:09,111
Let's see...

385
00:44:09,370 --> 00:44:13,699
I know! Hufflepuff!

386
00:44:15,458 --> 00:44:17,865
Ronald Weasley.

387
00:44:31,726 --> 00:44:36,720
Another Weasley!
I know just what to do with you.

388
00:44:37,440 --> 00:44:39,728
Gryffindor!

389
00:44:45,947 --> 00:44:48,439
Harry Potter.

390
00:45:06,509 --> 00:45:09,509
Difficult, very difficult.

391
00:45:09,721 --> 00:45:13,670
Plenty of courage, I see.
Not a bad mind, either.

392
00:45:13,892 --> 00:45:16,180
There's talent, oh, yes.

393
00:45:16,394 --> 00:45:20,226
And a thirst to prove yourself.

394
00:45:20,439 --> 00:45:22,598
But where to put you?

395
00:45:23,192 --> 00:45:25,682
Not Slytherin, not Slytherin!

396
00:45:25,945 --> 00:45:29,563
Not Slytherin, eh? Are you sure?

397
00:45:29,782 --> 00:45:34,657
You could be great, you know.
It's all here, in your head.

398
00:45:34,870 --> 00:45:40,208
And Slytherin will help you on the way
to greatness, no doubt about that.

399
00:45:40,542 --> 00:45:45,168
No? Well, if you're sure.

400
00:45:45,381 --> 00:45:47,124
Better be...

401
00:45:47,340 --> 00:45:49,298
...Gryffindor!

402
00:46:14,826 --> 00:46:17,613
Your attention, please.

403
00:46:19,665 --> 00:46:22,370
Let the feast begin.

404
00:46:39,309 --> 00:46:40,851
I'm half and half.

405
00:46:41,060 --> 00:46:44,310
Me dad's a Muggle. Mum's a witch.

406
00:46:44,522 --> 00:46:48,021
Bit of a nasty shock for him
when he found out.

407
00:46:49,026 --> 00:46:52,810
Percy, who's that teacher
talking to Professor Quirrell?

408
00:46:53,155 --> 00:46:56,274
Professor Snape,
head of Slytherin house.

409
00:46:56,492 --> 00:46:58,402
- What's he teach?
- Potions.

410
00:46:58,620 --> 00:47:04,206
But he fancies the Dark Arts.
He's been after Quirrell's job for years.

411
00:47:08,712 --> 00:47:11,037
Hello! How are you?

412
00:47:11,298 --> 00:47:14,667
Welcome to Gryffindor.

413
00:47:24,770 --> 00:47:27,261
It's the Bloody Baron!

414
00:47:31,903 --> 00:47:34,690
Hello, Sir Nicholas.
Have a nice summer?

415
00:47:34,906 --> 00:47:40,326
Dismal. Once again, my request to join
the Headless Hunt has been denied.

416
00:47:43,372 --> 00:47:46,289
I know you.
You're Nearly Headless Nick.

417
00:47:46,500 --> 00:47:49,252
I prefer Sir Nicholas,
if you don't mind.

418
00:47:49,461 --> 00:47:52,961
"Nearly" headless?
How can you be nearly headless?

419
00:47:53,298 --> 00:47:55,255
Like this.

420
00:48:05,268 --> 00:48:09,100
Gryffindors, follow me, please.
Keep up. Thank you.

421
00:48:09,314 --> 00:48:13,643
Ravenclaw, follow me. This way.

422
00:48:13,901 --> 00:48:17,235
This is the most direct path
to the dormitories.

423
00:48:17,447 --> 00:48:21,610
Keep an eye on the staircases.
They like to change.

424
00:48:30,751 --> 00:48:36,539
Keep up, please, and follow me.
Quickly now, come on. Come on.

425
00:48:36,757 --> 00:48:39,426
That picture's moving.

426
00:48:39,635 --> 00:48:43,134
- Look at that one.
- I think she fancies you.

427
00:48:44,891 --> 00:48:47,216
- Look!
- Who's that girl?

428
00:48:47,434 --> 00:48:49,972
Welcome to Hogwarts.

429
00:49:05,995 --> 00:49:07,572
Password?

430
00:49:08,038 --> 00:49:10,826
Caput Draconis.

431
00:49:17,589 --> 00:49:22,465
Follow me, everyone. Keep up.
Quickly, come on.

432
00:49:25,181 --> 00:49:27,588
Gather around here.

433
00:49:29,310 --> 00:49:32,594
Welcome to the Gryffindor common room.

434
00:49:32,813 --> 00:49:37,225
Boys' dormitory is upstairs to the left.
Girls, the same on your right.

435
00:49:37,442 --> 00:49:40,562
Your belongings have
already been brought up.

436
00:50:48,763 --> 00:50:50,387
Made it!

437
00:50:50,598 --> 00:50:55,010
Can you imagine the look on old
McGonagall's face if we were late?

438
00:50:58,272 --> 00:51:03,229
- That was bloody brilliant!
- Thank you for that assessment.

439
00:51:03,443 --> 00:51:07,737
It'd be better if I transfigured
Mr. Potter and you into a watch.

440
00:51:07,947 --> 00:51:11,151
- Then one of you might be on time.
- We got lost.

441
00:51:11,369 --> 00:51:17,122
Then perhaps a map? I trust you
don't need one to find your seats.

442
00:51:25,298 --> 00:51:30,968
There will be no foolish wand-waving
or silly incantations in this class.

443
00:51:31,179 --> 00:51:34,797
As such, I don't expect
many of you to appreciate...

444
00:51:35,058 --> 00:51:38,758
...the subtle science and exact art
that is potion-making.

445
00:51:38,978 --> 00:51:42,062
However, for those select few...

446
00:51:42,981 --> 00:51:46,315
...who possess the predisposition...

447
00:51:49,989 --> 00:51:53,275
...I can teach you
how to bewitch the mind...

448
00:51:53,493 --> 00:51:56,410
...and ensnare the senses.

449
00:51:56,621 --> 00:51:59,160
I can tell you how to bottle fame...

450
00:51:59,374 --> 00:52:05,293
...brew glory and even
put a stopper in death.

451
00:52:09,342 --> 00:52:14,217
Then again, maybe some of you have
come to Hogwarts with abilities...

452
00:52:14,429 --> 00:52:20,384
...so formidable that
you feel confident enough...

453
00:52:20,602 --> 00:52:23,556
...to not pay attention.

454
00:52:29,528 --> 00:52:32,102
Mr. Potter.

455
00:52:33,324 --> 00:52:37,156
Our new celebrity.

456
00:52:39,330 --> 00:52:45,118
What would I get if I added root
of asphodel to an infusion of wormwood?

457
00:52:48,380 --> 00:52:50,787
You don't know? Let's try again.

458
00:52:51,007 --> 00:52:55,633
Where would you look
if I asked you to find a bezoar?

459
00:52:56,930 --> 00:52:58,305
I don't know, sir.

460
00:52:58,599 --> 00:53:02,430
What is the difference
between monkshood and wolfsbane?

461
00:53:04,980 --> 00:53:07,221
I don't know, sir.

462
00:53:08,316 --> 00:53:09,596
Pity.

463
00:53:11,319 --> 00:53:15,530
Clearly, fame isn't everything...

464
00:53:16,282 --> 00:53:19,069
...is it, Mr. Potter?

465
00:53:21,245 --> 00:53:26,868
<i>Eye of rabbit, harp string hum
Turn this water into rum</i>

466
00:53:28,086 --> 00:53:29,627
<i>Eye of rabbit...</i>

467
00:53:29,962 --> 00:53:32,631
What's Seamus trying to do
to the water?

468
00:53:32,882 --> 00:53:37,591
Turn it to rum. Actually managed
a weak tea yesterday, before...

469
00:53:44,311 --> 00:53:46,219
Mail's here.

470
00:54:18,511 --> 00:54:21,464
Can I borrow this? Thanks.

471
00:54:25,392 --> 00:54:27,598
Look, Neville's got a Remembrall.

472
00:54:27,811 --> 00:54:33,315
I've read about those. The smoke turns
red when you've forgotten something.

473
00:54:33,691 --> 00:54:37,025
The problem is, I can't remember
what I've forgotten.

474
00:54:37,320 --> 00:54:40,735
Somebody broke into Gringotts. Listen.

475
00:54:40,948 --> 00:54:44,613
"Believed to be the work
of Dark wizards or witches...

476
00:54:44,869 --> 00:54:50,574
...Gringotts goblins acknowledge
the breach but insist nothing was taken.

477
00:54:50,792 --> 00:54:56,497
The vault in question, number 713,
had been emptied earlier that same day."

478
00:54:56,715 --> 00:55:00,962
That's odd. That's the vault
Hagrid and I went to.

479
00:55:09,895 --> 00:55:13,642
- Good afternoon, class.
- Good afternoon, Madam Hooch.

480
00:55:13,856 --> 00:55:16,643
Good afternoon, Amanda.
Good afternoon.

481
00:55:17,944 --> 00:55:20,399
Welcome to your first flying lesson.

482
00:55:20,613 --> 00:55:24,527
What are you waiting for?
Step up to your broomstick.

483
00:55:24,742 --> 00:55:30,330
Come on now, hurry up. Stick your hand
over the broom and say, "Up."

484
00:55:30,540 --> 00:55:32,496
Up!

485
00:55:32,750 --> 00:55:33,699
Up.

486
00:55:35,211 --> 00:55:37,038
Up.

487
00:55:38,714 --> 00:55:40,339
Up. Up!

488
00:55:40,549 --> 00:55:42,541
With feeling.

489
00:55:51,226 --> 00:55:53,349
Shut up, Harry.

490
00:55:53,603 --> 00:55:58,230
Now, once you've got hold of
your broom, I want you to mount it.

491
00:55:58,441 --> 00:56:02,439
Grip it tight. You don't wanna be
sliding off the end.

492
00:56:02,821 --> 00:56:07,779
When I blow my whistle, I want you
to kick off from the ground, hard.

493
00:56:07,993 --> 00:56:11,825
Keep your broom steady,
hover for a moment...

494
00:56:12,038 --> 00:56:16,332
...then lean forward slightly
and touch back down.

495
00:56:16,584 --> 00:56:19,704
On my whistle. Three, two...

496
00:56:22,131 --> 00:56:23,506
Mr. Longbottom.

497
00:56:28,138 --> 00:56:31,008
- Mr. Longbottom!
- Down, down!

498
00:56:31,224 --> 00:56:32,469
Neville!

499
00:56:36,188 --> 00:56:38,858
Come back down this instant!

500
00:57:07,843 --> 00:57:10,215
Everyone out of the way!

501
00:57:15,769 --> 00:57:17,927
Is he all right?

502
00:57:18,313 --> 00:57:23,983
Oh, dear, it's a broken wrist.
Poor boy. Come on now, up you get.

503
00:57:25,277 --> 00:57:29,939
Keep your feet on the ground
while I take him to the hospital wing.

504
00:57:30,156 --> 00:57:33,821
Understand? If I see
a single broom in the air...

505
00:57:34,035 --> 00:57:39,278
...the one riding it will be expelled
before they can say Quidditch.

506
00:57:39,499 --> 00:57:41,409
Did you see his face?

507
00:57:41,626 --> 00:57:45,458
If he had squeezed this, he'd have
remembered to fall on his arse.

508
00:57:45,672 --> 00:57:48,163
Give it here, Malfoy.

509
00:57:49,009 --> 00:57:52,709
No. I'll leave it somewhere
for Longbottom to find.

510
00:57:56,893 --> 00:57:59,347
How about on the roof?

511
00:58:00,521 --> 00:58:04,352
What's the matter, Potter?
Bit beyond your reach?

512
00:58:06,860 --> 00:58:10,692
Harry, no way!
You heard what Madam Hooch said.

513
00:58:10,906 --> 00:58:13,824
Besides, you don't know how to fly.

514
00:58:14,117 --> 00:58:16,026
What an idiot.

515
00:58:19,373 --> 00:58:22,907
Give it here or I'll
knock you off your broom!

516
00:58:23,126 --> 00:58:25,249
Is that so?

517
00:58:28,381 --> 00:58:30,670
Have it your way, then.

518
00:59:03,416 --> 00:59:07,034
- Nice going, Harry.
- That was wicked, Harry!

519
00:59:07,253 --> 00:59:09,292
Harry Potter!

520
00:59:10,256 --> 00:59:12,248
Follow me.

521
00:59:23,935 --> 00:59:26,177
You wait here.

522
00:59:27,940 --> 00:59:33,231
Professor Quirrell, excuse me.
Could I borrow Wood for a moment?

523
00:59:33,445 --> 00:59:35,272
Yes, of course.

524
00:59:40,954 --> 00:59:46,707
Potter, this is Oliver Wood.
Wood, I have found you a Seeker.

525
00:59:48,794 --> 00:59:52,293
Have you heard? Harry Potter's
the new Gryffindor Seeker.

526
00:59:52,548 --> 00:59:54,754
I always knew he'd do well.

527
00:59:55,217 --> 00:59:59,261
Seeker? But first years
never make the house teams.

528
00:59:59,471 --> 01:00:03,967
- You must be the youngest player in...
- A century, McGonagall says.

529
01:00:04,183 --> 01:00:06,805
Well done, Harry.
Wood's just told us.

530
01:00:07,020 --> 01:00:09,510
Fred and George are on the team.
Beaters.

531
01:00:09,730 --> 01:00:13,430
Our job is to make sure you
don't get bloodied up too bad.

532
01:00:13,651 --> 01:00:16,321
Can't make any promises.
Rough game, Quidditch.

533
01:00:16,530 --> 01:00:20,479
But no one's died in years.
Someone vanishes occasionally.

534
01:00:20,700 --> 01:00:23,452
But they'll turn up in a month or two.

535
01:00:23,703 --> 01:00:29,326
Go on. Quidditch is great. Best game
there is, and you'll be great too.

536
01:00:29,542 --> 01:00:32,744
I've never played.
What if I make a fool of myself?

537
01:00:33,170 --> 01:00:37,962
You won't make a fool of yourself.
It's in your blood.

538
01:00:46,516 --> 01:00:50,348
You never told me your father
was a Seeker too.

539
01:00:51,188 --> 01:00:53,394
I didn't know.

540
01:00:57,904 --> 01:01:02,483
I'm telling you, it's spooky.
She knows more about you than you do.

541
01:01:02,700 --> 01:01:04,988
Who doesn't?

542
01:01:05,912 --> 01:01:08,035
What's happening?

543
01:01:08,247 --> 01:01:12,458
The staircases change, remember?

544
01:01:17,922 --> 01:01:22,383
- Let's go this way.
- Before the staircase moves again.

545
01:01:30,018 --> 01:01:33,434
Does anybody feel like
we shouldn't be here?

546
01:01:33,688 --> 01:01:35,812
We're not supposed to be here.

547
01:01:36,024 --> 01:01:39,939
This is the third floor.
It's forbidden.

548
01:01:41,113 --> 01:01:42,690
Let's go.

549
01:01:44,908 --> 01:01:47,778
- It's Filch's cat!
- Run!

550
01:01:51,581 --> 01:01:54,914
Quick, let's hide through that door!

551
01:02:00,047 --> 01:02:02,087
- It's locked!
- We're done for!

552
01:02:02,300 --> 01:02:04,459
Move over!

553
01:02:05,428 --> 01:02:07,551
<i>Alohomora.</i>

554
01:02:08,431 --> 01:02:10,340
Get in.

555
01:02:11,600 --> 01:02:12,680
<i>Alohomora?</i>

556
01:02:12,894 --> 01:02:15,431
<i>Standard Book of Spells,
chapter seven.</i>

557
01:02:15,646 --> 01:02:19,015
Anyone here, my sweet?

558
01:02:25,281 --> 01:02:26,276
Come on.

559
01:02:27,157 --> 01:02:29,613
- Filch is gone.
- He thinks this door's locked.

560
01:02:29,869 --> 01:02:33,487
- It was locked.
- And for good reason.

561
01:02:59,190 --> 01:03:04,645
What are they doing, keeping a thing
like that locked up in a school?

562
01:03:04,861 --> 01:03:08,526
Didn't you see what
it was standing on?

563
01:03:08,740 --> 01:03:12,904
I wasn't looking at its feet!
I was preoccupied with its heads.

564
01:03:13,120 --> 01:03:15,990
Or maybe you didn't notice.
There were three!

565
01:03:16,206 --> 01:03:19,871
It was standing on a trap door.
It wasn't there by accident.

566
01:03:20,085 --> 01:03:23,619
- It's guarding something.
- Guarding something?

567
01:03:24,047 --> 01:03:27,795
That's right. Now, if you two don't mind,
I'm going to bed...

568
01:03:28,009 --> 01:03:31,627
...before you come up with another idea
to get us killed.

569
01:03:31,846 --> 01:03:34,966
Or worse, expelled.

570
01:03:38,227 --> 01:03:42,474
She needs to sort out her priorities.

571
01:03:47,110 --> 01:03:51,321
Quidditch is easy to understand.
Each team has seven players.

572
01:03:51,533 --> 01:03:57,238
Three Chasers, two Beaters,
one Keeper and a Seeker. That's you.

573
01:04:02,335 --> 01:04:06,463
There are three kinds of balls.
This one's called the Quaffle.

574
01:04:06,673 --> 01:04:12,627
The Chasers handle the Quaffle and try
to put it through one of those hoops.

575
01:04:12,845 --> 01:04:17,223
The Keeper, that's me,
defends the hoops. With me so far?

576
01:04:17,433 --> 01:04:21,893
I think so. What are those?

577
01:04:24,189 --> 01:04:26,347
You better take this.

578
01:04:36,410 --> 01:04:39,197
Careful now, it's coming back.

579
01:04:45,794 --> 01:04:49,412
Not bad, Potter.
You'd make a fair Beater.

580
01:05:06,065 --> 01:05:08,352
What was that?

581
01:05:09,109 --> 01:05:12,857
Bludger. Nasty little buggers.

582
01:05:13,070 --> 01:05:16,570
But you are a Seeker.

583
01:05:20,161 --> 01:05:24,739
The only thing I want you
to worry about is this.

584
01:05:24,998 --> 01:05:27,489
The Golden Snitch.

585
01:05:27,710 --> 01:05:30,710
- I like this ball.
- You like it now.

586
01:05:30,922 --> 01:05:34,920
Just wait. It's wicked fast
and damn near impossible to see.

587
01:05:35,134 --> 01:05:37,091
What do I do with it?

588
01:05:37,303 --> 01:05:40,553
You catch it.
Before the other team's Seeker.

589
01:05:40,808 --> 01:05:43,262
You catch this, the game's over.

590
01:05:43,476 --> 01:05:47,426
You catch this, Potter,
and we win.

591
01:05:56,489 --> 01:06:01,827
One of a wizard's most rudimentary
skills is levitation...

592
01:06:02,036 --> 01:06:05,985
...or the ability to make objects fly.

593
01:06:06,206 --> 01:06:08,613
Do you have your feathers? Good.

594
01:06:08,876 --> 01:06:14,000
Now, don't forget the nice wrist
movement we've been practicing.

595
01:06:14,215 --> 01:06:17,548
The swish and flick. Everyone.

596
01:06:18,094 --> 01:06:23,716
The swish and flick. Good.
Oh, and enunciate.

597
01:06:24,432 --> 01:06:28,726
<i>Wingardium Leviosa.
Off you go, then.</i>

598
01:06:29,771 --> 01:06:32,262
<i>Wingardium Leviosa.</i>

599
01:06:32,524 --> 01:06:34,849
<i>Wingardium Leviosa.</i>

600
01:06:38,696 --> 01:06:42,943
No, stop, stop, stop! You're going
to take someone's eye out.

601
01:06:43,200 --> 01:06:49,155
<i>Besides, you're saying it wrong.
It's Leviosa, not Leviosar.</i>

602
01:06:49,748 --> 01:06:53,959
You do it then, if you're so clever.
Go on, go on.

603
01:06:55,213 --> 01:06:58,297
<i>Wingardium Leviosa.</i>

604
01:07:05,807 --> 01:07:11,431
Well done! See here, everyone,
Miss Granger's done it!

605
01:07:11,646 --> 01:07:13,306
Splendid!

606
01:07:14,899 --> 01:07:17,105
Well done, dear.

607
01:07:21,321 --> 01:07:25,402
I think we're going to need
another feather over here.

608
01:07:31,916 --> 01:07:36,163
<i>"It's Leviosa, not Leviosar."</i>

609
01:07:36,420 --> 01:07:41,759
She's a nightmare, honestly!
No wonder she hasn't got any friends.

610
01:07:42,426 --> 01:07:44,964
I think she heard you.

611
01:08:13,623 --> 01:08:15,700
Where's Hermione?

612
01:08:15,918 --> 01:08:19,036
Parvati said she wouldn't
come out of the bathroom.

613
01:08:19,254 --> 01:08:23,334
She said that she'd been in there
all afternoon, crying.

614
01:08:27,761 --> 01:08:31,426
Troll in the dungeon!

615
01:08:31,684 --> 01:08:35,016
Troll in the dungeon!

616
01:08:37,814 --> 01:08:40,139
Thought you ought to know.

617
01:08:47,032 --> 01:08:49,867
Silence!

618
01:08:51,452 --> 01:08:55,497
Everyone will please not panic!

619
01:08:56,165 --> 01:08:57,743
Now...

620
01:08:57,959 --> 01:09:02,501
...prefects will lead their house
back to the dormitories.

621
01:09:03,213 --> 01:09:08,006
Teachers will follow me
to the dungeons.

622
01:09:19,063 --> 01:09:22,230
Gryffindors, keep up, please,
and stay alert.

623
01:09:22,441 --> 01:09:24,185
How could a troll get in?

624
01:09:24,402 --> 01:09:29,562
Not on its own. Trolls are really stupid.
Probably people playing jokes.

625
01:09:29,782 --> 01:09:33,780
- What?
- Hermione! She doesn't know.

626
01:09:45,881 --> 01:09:49,130
I think the troll's left the dungeon.

627
01:09:53,013 --> 01:09:55,171
It's going into the girls' bathroom.

628
01:10:26,212 --> 01:10:28,584
Hermione, move!

629
01:10:31,968 --> 01:10:36,096
Help! Help!

630
01:10:38,099 --> 01:10:40,175
Hey, pea brain!

631
01:10:52,613 --> 01:10:54,486
Help!

632
01:11:15,635 --> 01:11:18,008
Do something!

633
01:11:19,431 --> 01:11:23,381
- What?
- Anything!

634
01:11:24,018 --> 01:11:26,426
- Hurry up!
- Swish and flick.

635
01:11:26,646 --> 01:11:28,971
<i>Wingardium Leviosa.</i>

636
01:11:39,911 --> 01:11:41,903
Cool.

637
01:12:06,310 --> 01:12:09,145
Is it dead?

638
01:12:09,355 --> 01:12:13,269
I don't think so. Just knocked out.

639
01:12:19,532 --> 01:12:21,857
Troll boogers.

640
01:12:24,370 --> 01:12:27,905
Oh, my goodness!
Explain yourselves, both of you!

641
01:12:28,124 --> 01:12:32,750
- Well, what it is...
- It's my fault, Professor McGonagall.

642
01:12:34,922 --> 01:12:36,120
Miss Granger?

643
01:12:37,007 --> 01:12:42,084
I went looking for the troll.
I thought I could handle it.

644
01:12:42,304 --> 01:12:44,178
But I was wrong.

645
01:12:44,389 --> 01:12:49,430
If Harry and Ron hadn't come
and found me, I'd probably be dead.

646
01:12:50,436 --> 01:12:54,849
Be that as it may, it was
an extremely foolish thing to do.

647
01:12:55,067 --> 01:13:00,737
I expected more rational behavior
and am very disappointed in you.

648
01:13:00,948 --> 01:13:03,949
Five points will be taken
from Gryffindor...

649
01:13:04,160 --> 01:13:07,742
...for your serious lack of judgment.

650
01:13:08,205 --> 01:13:10,198
As for you two gentlemen...

651
01:13:10,416 --> 01:13:13,832
...I just hope you realize
how fortunate you are.

652
01:13:14,044 --> 01:13:17,460
Not many first-year students
could take on a troll...

653
01:13:17,672 --> 01:13:20,294
...and live to tell the tale.

654
01:13:20,551 --> 01:13:22,958
Five points...

655
01:13:24,345 --> 01:13:27,465
...will be awarded to each of you...

656
01:13:29,059 --> 01:13:32,144
...for sheer dumb luck.

657
01:13:37,734 --> 01:13:41,482
Perhaps you ought to go.
It might wake up.

658
01:13:49,356 --> 01:13:52,108
Take a bit of toast, mate. Go on.

659
01:13:52,318 --> 01:13:55,520
Ron's right.
You'll need your strength today.

660
01:13:55,738 --> 01:13:57,944
I'm not hungry.

661
01:13:58,532 --> 01:14:04,155
Good luck today, Potter.
You've proven yourself against a troll.

662
01:14:04,371 --> 01:14:07,538
A game of Quidditch
should be easy work.

663
01:14:07,750 --> 01:14:10,870
Even if it is against Slytherin.

664
01:14:18,552 --> 01:14:21,968
- That explains the blood.
- Blood?

665
01:14:22,389 --> 01:14:26,517
Last night, I'm guessing Snape let
the troll in as a diversion...

666
01:14:26,726 --> 01:14:29,396
...so he could get past that dog.

667
01:14:29,604 --> 01:14:32,356
But he got bit,
that's why he's limping.

668
01:14:32,608 --> 01:14:34,814
But why would anyone go near that dog?

669
01:14:35,485 --> 01:14:38,736
At Gringotts, Hagrid took
something out of the vault.

670
01:14:38,947 --> 01:14:42,197
Said it was Hogwarts business,
very secret.

671
01:14:42,410 --> 01:14:43,524
You're saying...

672
01:14:43,745 --> 01:14:48,240
That's what the dog's guarding.
That's what Snape wants.

673
01:15:01,387 --> 01:15:05,335
- Bit early for mail, isn't it?
- But I never get mail.

674
01:15:05,890 --> 01:15:07,433
Let's open it.

675
01:15:17,610 --> 01:15:18,856
It's a broomstick.

676
01:15:19,654 --> 01:15:23,782
That's not just a broomstick,
it's a Nimbus 2000!

677
01:15:25,243 --> 01:15:27,282
But who?

678
01:15:48,932 --> 01:15:51,423
- Scared, Harry?
- A little.

679
01:15:51,643 --> 01:15:55,308
It's all right. I felt the same way
before my first game.

680
01:15:55,522 --> 01:15:59,022
- What happened?
- I don't really remember.

681
01:15:59,318 --> 01:16:01,987
I took a Bludger to the head
two minutes in.

682
01:16:02,196 --> 01:16:05,031
Woke up in hospital a week later.

683
01:16:27,220 --> 01:16:30,589
Welcome to Hogwarts' first
Quidditch game of the season.

684
01:16:30,808 --> 01:16:35,517
Today's game,
Slytherin versus Gryffindor!

685
01:17:05,801 --> 01:17:08,256
The players take their positions...

686
01:17:08,470 --> 01:17:12,254
...as Madam Hooch steps onto
the field to begin the game!

687
01:17:12,474 --> 01:17:15,807
Now, I want a nice, clean game...

688
01:17:16,435 --> 01:17:18,843
...from all of you!

689
01:17:23,984 --> 01:17:26,902
The Bludgers are up,
followed by the Golden Snitch.

690
01:17:27,112 --> 01:17:29,817
Remember, the Snitch
is worth 150 points.

691
01:17:30,031 --> 01:17:33,815
The Seeker who catches the Snitch
ends the game.

692
01:17:39,958 --> 01:17:44,087
The Quaffle is released
and the game begins!

693
01:18:02,773 --> 01:18:07,565
Angelina Johnson scores!
Ten points for Gryffindor!

694
01:18:12,741 --> 01:18:14,021
Well done!

695
01:18:18,413 --> 01:18:24,119
Slytherin takes the Quaffle.
Bletchley passes to Captain Marcus Flint.

696
01:18:56,158 --> 01:18:58,946
Another 10 points to Gryffindor!

697
01:19:12,758 --> 01:19:14,632
Give me that!

698
01:19:46,083 --> 01:19:48,705
Take that side!

699
01:20:38,176 --> 01:20:41,426
What's going on
with Harry's broomstick?

700
01:20:50,355 --> 01:20:52,561
It's Snape.
He's jinxing the broom!

701
01:20:52,774 --> 01:20:57,151
- Jinxing the broom? What do we do?
- Leave it to me.

702
01:21:18,924 --> 01:21:20,466
Come on, Hermione!

703
01:21:34,564 --> 01:21:38,313
<i>Lacarnum Inflamarae.</i>

704
01:21:45,408 --> 01:21:48,444
Fire! You're on fire!

705
01:22:06,304 --> 01:22:08,463
Go, go, go, go!

706
01:23:00,482 --> 01:23:02,807
Looks like he's gonna be sick.

707
01:23:03,901 --> 01:23:05,360
He's got the Snitch!

708
01:23:05,570 --> 01:23:09,650
Harry Potter receives 150 points
for catching the Snitch!

709
01:23:09,867 --> 01:23:11,527
Gryffindor wins!

710
01:23:55,119 --> 01:23:59,367
Nonsense! Why would Snape
put a curse on Harry's broom?

711
01:23:59,582 --> 01:24:03,496
Who knows? Why was he trying
to get past that three-headed dog?

712
01:24:03,712 --> 01:24:06,118
- Who told you about Fluffy?
- Fluffy?

713
01:24:06,338 --> 01:24:10,003
- That thing has a name?
- Of course he has a name. He's mine.

714
01:24:10,217 --> 01:24:15,508
I bought him off an Irishman.
I lent him to Dumbledore to guard...

715
01:24:15,722 --> 01:24:20,301
Shouldn't have said that.
No more questions! That's top-secret.

716
01:24:20,895 --> 01:24:24,893
But whatever Fluffy's guarding,
Snape's trying to steal it.

717
01:24:25,107 --> 01:24:28,559
Codswallop. Professor Snape
is a Hogwarts teacher.

718
01:24:29,070 --> 01:24:34,146
Teacher or not, I know a spell when
I see one. I've read all about them.

719
01:24:34,366 --> 01:24:37,949
You've got to keep eye contact,
and Snape wasn't blinking.

720
01:24:38,162 --> 01:24:40,403
Exactly.

721
01:24:41,081 --> 01:24:43,833
Now, you listen to me,
all three of you.

722
01:24:44,042 --> 01:24:48,704
You're meddling in things that ought
not to be meddled in. It's dangerous.

723
01:24:48,922 --> 01:24:53,998
What that dog is guarding is
between Dumbledore and Nicholas Flamel.

724
01:24:54,219 --> 01:24:55,629
Nicholas Flamel?

725
01:24:56,638 --> 01:25:01,347
I shouldn't have said that.
I should not have said that.

726
01:25:01,559 --> 01:25:05,640
Nicholas Flamel.
Who's Nicholas Flamel?

727
01:25:05,856 --> 01:25:07,849
I don't know.

728
01:25:26,709 --> 01:25:29,544
<i>Merry Christmas
Merry Christmas</i>

729
01:25:29,795 --> 01:25:32,582
<i>Ring the Hogwart bell</i>

730
01:25:32,799 --> 01:25:35,586
<i>Merry Christmas
Merry Christmas</i>

731
01:25:35,802 --> 01:25:38,720
<i>Cast a Christmas spell</i>

732
01:25:52,318 --> 01:25:55,652
Knight to e5.

733
01:26:03,328 --> 01:26:05,486
Queen to e5.

734
01:26:11,129 --> 01:26:12,539
That's totally barbaric!

735
01:26:13,172 --> 01:26:16,706
That's wizard's chess.
I see you've packed.

736
01:26:16,925 --> 01:26:18,384
I see you haven't.

737
01:26:18,760 --> 01:26:23,885
Change of plans. My parents went
to Romania to visit my brother Charlie.

738
01:26:24,099 --> 01:26:27,931
- He's studying dragons there.
- Good. You can help Harry.

739
01:26:28,144 --> 01:26:31,513
He's going to the library
to look up Nicholas Flamel.

740
01:26:31,731 --> 01:26:35,230
We've looked a hundred times!

741
01:26:35,860 --> 01:26:41,103
Not in the restricted section.
Happy Christmas.

742
01:26:43,327 --> 01:26:46,244
I think we've had
a bad influence on her.

743
01:26:48,791 --> 01:26:53,120
Harry, wake up!
Come on, Harry, wake up!

744
01:27:02,971 --> 01:27:06,305
- Happy Christmas, Harry.
- Happy Christmas, Ron.

745
01:27:06,516 --> 01:27:08,722
What are you wearing?

746
01:27:09,310 --> 01:27:13,011
Oh, my mum made it.
Looks like you've got one too.

747
01:27:14,148 --> 01:27:16,556
- I've got presents?
- Yeah.

748
01:27:23,992 --> 01:27:26,067
There they are.

749
01:27:37,088 --> 01:27:40,587
"Your father left this
in my possession before he died.

750
01:27:40,841 --> 01:27:44,969
It is time it was returned to you.
Use it well."

751
01:28:01,779 --> 01:28:05,479
- What is it?
- Some kind of cloak.

752
01:28:05,783 --> 01:28:08,699
Well, let's see, then. Put it on.

753
01:28:14,125 --> 01:28:15,404
My body's gone!

754
01:28:15,626 --> 01:28:19,209
I know what that is.
That's an invisibility cloak!

755
01:28:19,755 --> 01:28:21,664
I'm invisible?

756
01:28:22,132 --> 01:28:26,545
They're really rare.
I wonder who gave it to you.

757
01:28:27,011 --> 01:28:31,804
There was no name.
It just said, "Use it well."

758
01:28:59,877 --> 01:29:05,749
<i>Famous Fire-Eaters.
Fifteenth-Century Fiends.</i>

759
01:29:05,966 --> 01:29:11,802
Flamel. Nicholas Flamel.
Where are you?

760
01:29:30,615 --> 01:29:32,525
Who's there?

761
01:29:38,666 --> 01:29:44,289
I know you're in there.
You can't hide.

762
01:29:51,679 --> 01:29:55,427
Who is it? Show yourself.

763
01:30:42,603 --> 01:30:43,978
Severus, I...

764
01:30:44,647 --> 01:30:48,514
You don't want me
as your enemy, Quirrell.

765
01:30:48,734 --> 01:30:53,443
- I don't know what you mean.
- You know perfectly well what I mean.

766
01:31:10,673 --> 01:31:13,877
We'll have another little chat soon.

767
01:31:14,094 --> 01:31:19,549
When you've had time to decide
where your loyalties lie.

768
01:31:19,807 --> 01:31:24,219
Professors. I found this
in the restricted section.

769
01:31:24,770 --> 01:31:29,811
It's still hot. That means
there's a student out of bed.

770
01:33:01,907 --> 01:33:03,734
Mum?

771
01:33:06,995 --> 01:33:08,988
Dad?

772
01:33:43,739 --> 01:33:48,698
Ron, you've really gotta see this!
Ron, you've gotta see this!

773
01:33:50,538 --> 01:33:53,408
Ron, come on, get out of bed!

774
01:33:53,624 --> 01:33:57,207
- Why?
- There's something you've got to see!

775
01:34:03,927 --> 01:34:08,220
Come on! Come!
Come look, it's my parents!

776
01:34:09,683 --> 01:34:11,640
I only see us.

777
01:34:11,893 --> 01:34:15,227
Look in properly.
Go on, stand there.

778
01:34:15,438 --> 01:34:21,357
- There. You see them, don't you?
- That's me! Only I'm head boy.

779
01:34:21,861 --> 01:34:24,186
And I'm holding the Quidditch Cup.

780
01:34:24,447 --> 01:34:28,610
And bloody hell!
I'm Quidditch captain too!

781
01:34:29,743 --> 01:34:32,199
I look good.

782
01:34:32,830 --> 01:34:36,662
Harry, do you think this mirror
shows the future?

783
01:34:36,876 --> 01:34:41,834
How can it?
Both my parents are dead.

784
01:35:04,986 --> 01:35:07,144
Back again, Harry?

785
01:35:10,242 --> 01:35:12,732
I see that you,
like many before you...

786
01:35:12,953 --> 01:35:17,117
...have discovered the delights
of the Mirror of Erised.

787
01:35:17,458 --> 01:35:21,621
I trust by now
you realize what it does.

788
01:35:22,921 --> 01:35:25,458
Let me give you a clue.

789
01:35:26,008 --> 01:35:28,130
The happiest man on earth...

790
01:35:28,342 --> 01:35:31,712
...would look in the mirror
and see only himself...

791
01:35:31,929 --> 01:35:34,254
...exactly as he is.

792
01:35:34,473 --> 01:35:39,514
So then, it shows us what we want.
Whatever we want.

793
01:35:39,729 --> 01:35:42,481
Yes. And no.

794
01:35:43,525 --> 01:35:45,980
It shows us nothing more or less...

795
01:35:46,194 --> 01:35:52,149
...than the deepest and most desperate
desires of our hearts.

796
01:35:52,368 --> 01:35:57,076
Now you, Harry, who have
never known your family...

797
01:35:57,289 --> 01:36:01,156
...you see them standing beside you.

798
01:36:01,376 --> 01:36:03,783
But remember this, Harry.

799
01:36:04,045 --> 01:36:09,917
This mirror gives us
neither knowledge...

800
01:36:10,134 --> 01:36:12,257
...or truth.

801
01:36:13,221 --> 01:36:19,258
Men have wasted away in front of it.
Even gone mad.

802
01:36:20,310 --> 01:36:24,439
That is why tomorrow
it will be moved to a new home.

803
01:36:24,649 --> 01:36:26,558
And I must ask you...

804
01:36:27,526 --> 01:36:31,393
...not to go looking for it again.

805
01:36:32,156 --> 01:36:35,275
It does not do to dwell on dreams...

806
01:36:35,868 --> 01:36:38,738
...and forget to live.

807
01:37:33,466 --> 01:37:39,136
I had you looking in the wrong section.
How could I be so stupid?

808
01:37:39,389 --> 01:37:42,474
I checked this out weeks ago
for a bit of light reading.

809
01:37:42,684 --> 01:37:44,676
This is light?

810
01:37:49,273 --> 01:37:51,681
Of course! Here it is!

811
01:37:51,901 --> 01:37:55,899
Nicholas Flamel is the only known
maker of the Philosopher's Stone.

812
01:37:56,155 --> 01:37:57,317
The what?

813
01:37:57,990 --> 01:38:00,991
Honestly, don't you two read?

814
01:38:01,201 --> 01:38:05,697
"The Philosopher's Stone is a legendary
substance with astonishing powers.

815
01:38:05,914 --> 01:38:08,535
It'll transform any metal
into pure gold...

816
01:38:08,750 --> 01:38:12,748
...and produces the Elixir of Life
which will make the drinker immortal."

817
01:38:12,962 --> 01:38:15,120
- Immortal?
- It means you'll never die.

818
01:38:15,340 --> 01:38:17,417
I know what it means!

819
01:38:18,302 --> 01:38:23,010
"The only Stone currently in existence
belongs to Mr. Nicholas Flamel...

820
01:38:23,223 --> 01:38:28,383
...the noted alchemist who last year
celebrated his 665th birthday."

821
01:38:30,104 --> 01:38:32,262
That's what Fluffy's guarding.

822
01:38:32,482 --> 01:38:37,191
That's what's under the trap door.
The Philosopher's Stone.

823
01:38:53,962 --> 01:38:57,746
Don't wish to be rude,
but I'm in no state to entertain.

824
01:38:57,966 --> 01:39:00,671
We know about the Philosopher's Stone.

825
01:39:05,391 --> 01:39:10,514
- We think Snape's trying to steal it.
- Are you still on about him?

826
01:39:10,728 --> 01:39:13,515
We know he's after it.
We don't know why.

827
01:39:13,898 --> 01:39:18,061
Snape is one of the teachers
protecting the Stone. He won't steal it.

828
01:39:18,319 --> 01:39:19,398
What?

829
01:39:19,570 --> 01:39:22,985
You heard. Come on,
I'm a bit preoccupied today.

830
01:39:23,199 --> 01:39:25,868
Wait a minute.
"One of the teachers"?

831
01:39:26,077 --> 01:39:29,944
There are other things
defending the Stone, aren't there?

832
01:39:30,164 --> 01:39:32,786
- Spells, enchantments.
- Right.

833
01:39:33,042 --> 01:39:36,079
Waste of bloody time, if you ask me.

834
01:39:36,296 --> 01:39:38,371
Ain't no one gonna get past Fluffy.

835
01:39:38,589 --> 01:39:42,254
Ain't a soul knows how,
except for me and Dumbledore.

836
01:39:42,510 --> 01:39:46,092
I shouldn't have told you that.
I should not have told you that.

837
01:39:59,943 --> 01:40:05,019
- Hagrid, what exactly is that?
- That? It's...

838
01:40:05,282 --> 01:40:07,274
I know what that is!

839
01:40:07,493 --> 01:40:10,113
But, Hagrid, how did you get one?

840
01:40:10,495 --> 01:40:13,745
I won it. Off a stranger
I met down at the pub.

841
01:40:13,958 --> 01:40:18,038
Seemed quite glad to be rid of it,
as a matter of fact.

842
01:40:40,276 --> 01:40:42,482
Is that...

843
01:40:43,278 --> 01:40:44,441
...a dragon?

844
01:40:44,655 --> 01:40:49,067
That's not just a dragon.
That's a Norwegian Ridgeback.

845
01:40:49,284 --> 01:40:52,155
My brother works
with these in Romania.

846
01:40:52,370 --> 01:40:57,246
Isn't he beautiful? Oh, bless him.
Look, he knows his mummy.

847
01:40:57,917 --> 01:40:59,661
Hello, Norbert.

848
01:41:00,002 --> 01:41:04,296
- Norbert?
- He's gotta have a name, don't he?

849
01:41:05,048 --> 01:41:07,504
Don't you, Norbert?

850
01:41:14,476 --> 01:41:17,595
He'll have to be trained up a bit,
of course.

851
01:41:21,482 --> 01:41:23,558
Who's that?

852
01:41:25,277 --> 01:41:27,354
Malfoy.

853
01:41:28,113 --> 01:41:29,523
Oh, dear.

854
01:41:31,241 --> 01:41:36,033
Hagrid always wanted a dragon.
Told me so the first time I met him.

855
01:41:36,246 --> 01:41:40,290
It's crazy.
And worse, Malfoy knows.

856
01:41:40,500 --> 01:41:44,580
- I don't understand. Is that bad?
- It's bad.

857
01:41:44,880 --> 01:41:47,039
Good evening.

858
01:41:50,678 --> 01:41:53,596
Nothing, I repeat, nothing...

859
01:41:53,848 --> 01:41:57,347
...gives a student the right
to walk about at night.

860
01:41:57,559 --> 01:42:02,435
Therefore, as punishment for your actions,
50 points will be taken.

861
01:42:02,648 --> 01:42:04,973
- 50?!
- Each.

862
01:42:06,026 --> 01:42:08,398
To ensure it doesn't happen again...

863
01:42:08,612 --> 01:42:11,945
...all four of you
will receive detention.

864
01:42:12,865 --> 01:42:15,819
Excuse me, professor,
perhaps I heard you wrong.

865
01:42:16,035 --> 01:42:18,360
I thought you said the four of us.

866
01:42:18,580 --> 01:42:21,071
No, you heard me correctly.

867
01:42:21,291 --> 01:42:26,285
Honorable as your intentions were,
you too were out of bed after hours.

868
01:42:26,755 --> 01:42:29,709
You will join your classmates
in detention.

869
01:42:40,935 --> 01:42:44,933
A pity they let
the old punishments die.

870
01:42:45,148 --> 01:42:49,856
Was a time detention found you
hanging by your thumbs in the dungeons.

871
01:42:50,069 --> 01:42:52,904
God, I miss the screaming.

872
01:42:55,449 --> 01:42:58,734
You'll be serving detention
with Hagrid tonight.

873
01:42:58,952 --> 01:43:04,291
He's got a little job to do
inside the Dark Forest.

874
01:43:06,376 --> 01:43:09,331
A sorry lot, this, Hagrid.

875
01:43:10,798 --> 01:43:15,792
Good God, you're not still on
about that bloody dragon, are you?

876
01:43:18,056 --> 01:43:20,131
Norbert's gone.

877
01:43:20,683 --> 01:43:24,218
Dumbledore sent him off to Romania
to live in a colony.

878
01:43:24,520 --> 01:43:27,770
That's good, isn't it?
He's with his own kind.

879
01:43:27,940 --> 01:43:30,265
What if he don't like Romania?

880
01:43:30,484 --> 01:43:34,730
What if the other dragons are mean
to him? He's only a baby.

881
01:43:35,364 --> 01:43:40,606
For God's sake, pull yourself together.
You're going into the Forest.

882
01:43:40,828 --> 01:43:43,200
Got to have your wits about you.

883
01:43:43,414 --> 01:43:49,084
The Forest? I thought that was a joke.
We can't go in there.

884
01:43:49,544 --> 01:43:53,376
Students aren't allowed.
And there are...

885
01:43:54,925 --> 01:43:56,169
...werewolves.

886
01:43:56,592 --> 01:43:59,878
There's more than werewolves
in those trees.

887
01:44:00,096 --> 01:44:02,765
You can be sure of that.

888
01:44:04,726 --> 01:44:06,136
Nighty-night.

889
01:44:08,730 --> 01:44:11,565
Right. Let's go.

890
01:44:49,770 --> 01:44:52,178
Hagrid, what is that?

891
01:44:52,399 --> 01:44:55,767
What we're here for.
See that?

892
01:44:56,277 --> 01:45:01,651
That's unicorn blood, that is.
I found one dead a few weeks ago.

893
01:45:02,199 --> 01:45:06,778
Now, this one's been hurt bad
by something.

894
01:45:14,294 --> 01:45:20,048
So, it's our job to go
and find the poor beast.

895
01:45:20,258 --> 01:45:23,378
Ron, Hermione, come with me.

896
01:45:23,845 --> 01:45:27,130
And, Harry, you'll go with Malfoy.

897
01:45:28,392 --> 01:45:30,680
Okay. Then I get Fang.

898
01:45:30,853 --> 01:45:36,606
Fine. Just so you know,
he's a bloody coward.

899
01:45:40,278 --> 01:45:45,272
Wait till my father hears about this.
This is servant's stuff.

900
01:45:45,491 --> 01:45:49,406
If I didn't know better,
I'd say you were scared.

901
01:45:49,621 --> 01:45:52,193
I'm not scared, Potter.

902
01:45:53,332 --> 01:45:55,290
Do you hear that?

903
01:45:57,837 --> 01:45:59,247
Come on, Fang.

904
01:45:59,462 --> 01:46:00,958
Scared!

905
01:46:25,948 --> 01:46:28,106
What is it, Fang?

906
01:47:38,477 --> 01:47:43,981
Harry Potter, you must leave.
You are known to many creatures here.

907
01:47:44,192 --> 01:47:48,189
The Forest is not safe at this time.
Especially for you.

908
01:47:48,405 --> 01:47:51,156
What was that thing you saved me from?

909
01:47:51,365 --> 01:47:56,704
A monstrous creature.
It is a terrible crime to slay a unicorn.

910
01:47:56,913 --> 01:48:02,453
Drinking its blood will keep you alive
even if you are an inch from death.

911
01:48:02,668 --> 01:48:07,745
But at a terrible price. For you
have slain something so pure...

912
01:48:07,965 --> 01:48:12,793
...that the moment the blood touches
your lips, you will have a half-life.

913
01:48:13,012 --> 01:48:14,803
A cursed life.

914
01:48:15,014 --> 01:48:18,963
- Who would choose such a life?
- Can you think of no one?

915
01:48:19,184 --> 01:48:24,143
Do you mean to say that
that thing that killed the unicorn...

916
01:48:24,481 --> 01:48:28,395
...that was drinking its blood,
that was Voldemort?

917
01:48:28,611 --> 01:48:33,771
Do you know what is hidden
in the school at this very moment?

918
01:48:34,617 --> 01:48:36,159
The Philosopher's Stone.

919
01:48:37,494 --> 01:48:39,487
Harry!

920
01:48:40,080 --> 01:48:44,576
Hello there, Firenze.
See you've met our young Mr. Potter.

921
01:48:44,792 --> 01:48:46,952
You all right there, Harry?

922
01:48:48,088 --> 01:48:52,382
Harry Potter,
this is where I leave you.

923
01:48:53,259 --> 01:48:57,091
You're safe now. Good luck.

924
01:49:04,728 --> 01:49:08,856
You mean, You-Know-Who is out there
right now in the Forest?

925
01:49:09,067 --> 01:49:11,854
But he's weak.
He's living off the unicorns.

926
01:49:12,070 --> 01:49:14,987
Don't you see? We had it wrong.

927
01:49:15,199 --> 01:49:19,576
Snape doesn't want the Stone for himself.
He wants it for Voldemort.

928
01:49:19,786 --> 01:49:24,329
With the Elixir of Life,
Voldemort will be strong again.

929
01:49:24,541 --> 01:49:26,118
He'll come back.

930
01:49:26,334 --> 01:49:28,078
But if he comes back...

931
01:49:28,336 --> 01:49:32,286
...you don't think he'll try
to kill you, do you?

932
01:49:33,299 --> 01:49:36,834
If he'd had the chance,
he might have tried tonight.

933
01:49:37,053 --> 01:49:40,635
And to think I've been worrying
about my Potions final.

934
01:49:40,847 --> 01:49:44,431
Hang on a minute.
We're forgetting one thing.

935
01:49:44,811 --> 01:49:49,686
Who's the one wizard
Voldemort always feared?

936
01:49:50,442 --> 01:49:55,566
Dumbledore. As long as Dumbledore
is around, Harry, you're safe.

937
01:49:55,779 --> 01:49:59,824
As long as Dumbledore is around,
you can't be touched.

938
01:50:05,581 --> 01:50:11,001
I'd heard Hogwarts' final exams were
frightful, but I found that enjoyable.

939
01:50:11,211 --> 01:50:14,876
Speak for yourself.
All right there, Harry?

940
01:50:15,089 --> 01:50:20,249
- My scar. It keeps burning.
- It's happened before.

941
01:50:20,470 --> 01:50:23,139
- Not like this.
- You should see the nurse.

942
01:50:23,349 --> 01:50:26,848
I think it's a warning.
It means danger's coming.

943
01:50:34,484 --> 01:50:36,940
- Of course!
- What is it?

944
01:50:37,153 --> 01:50:40,901
Isn't it odd that what Hagrid wants
more than anything is a dragon...

945
01:50:41,115 --> 01:50:44,199
...and a stranger just happens
to have one?

946
01:50:44,411 --> 01:50:47,080
How many people wander around
with dragon eggs?

947
01:50:47,288 --> 01:50:49,531
Why didn't I see it before?

948
01:50:55,130 --> 01:50:58,630
Who gave you the egg?
What did he look like?

949
01:50:58,842 --> 01:51:01,594
I never saw his face.
He kept his hood up.

950
01:51:01,804 --> 01:51:04,376
You and this stranger
must have talked.

951
01:51:04,973 --> 01:51:08,508
He wanted to know what sort
of creatures I looked after.

952
01:51:08,727 --> 01:51:12,724
I said, "After Fluffy,
a dragon's gonna be no problem."

953
01:51:12,939 --> 01:51:17,400
- Was he interested in Fluffy?
- Of course he was interested.

954
01:51:17,818 --> 01:51:21,982
How often do you come across
a three-headed dog?

955
01:51:22,197 --> 01:51:27,821
But I told him, "The trick with any beast
is to know how to calm him."

956
01:51:28,036 --> 01:51:33,493
Take Fluffy, for example. Play him
music and he falls straight to sleep.

957
01:51:35,127 --> 01:51:37,833
I shouldn't have told you that.

958
01:51:38,089 --> 01:51:40,295
Where are you going?

959
01:51:47,306 --> 01:51:50,057
We have to see Dumbledore.
Immediately!

960
01:51:50,517 --> 01:51:53,139
I'm afraid he's not here.

961
01:51:53,353 --> 01:51:57,646
He received an urgent owl
from the Ministry of Magic and left.

962
01:51:58,066 --> 01:52:00,603
He's gone?
But this is important!

963
01:52:00,861 --> 01:52:03,067
This is about the Philosopher's Stone!

964
01:52:04,989 --> 01:52:08,689
- How do you know?
- Someone's going to try and steal it.

965
01:52:09,328 --> 01:52:14,534
I don't know how you know,
but I assure you it is well protected.

966
01:52:14,749 --> 01:52:19,043
Now would you go back
to your dormitories? Quietly.

967
01:52:27,345 --> 01:52:30,132
That was no stranger Hagrid met.
It was Snape.

968
01:52:30,348 --> 01:52:33,017
Which means he knows
how to get past Fluffy.

969
01:52:33,226 --> 01:52:37,094
- And with Dumbledore gone...
- Good afternoon.

970
01:52:39,149 --> 01:52:42,232
What would three young Gryffindors...

971
01:52:42,486 --> 01:52:46,779
...be doing inside on a day like this?

972
01:52:51,536 --> 01:52:55,071
- We were just...
- You ought to be careful.

973
01:52:55,623 --> 01:52:57,581
People will think you're...

974
01:53:01,879 --> 01:53:04,583
...up to something.

975
01:53:14,892 --> 01:53:16,884
Now what do we do?

976
01:53:17,102 --> 01:53:20,850
We go down the trap door. Tonight.

977
01:53:34,619 --> 01:53:36,078
Trevor.

978
01:53:36,413 --> 01:53:39,828
Trevor, go! You shouldn't be here!

979
01:53:40,083 --> 01:53:45,504
Neither should you.
You're sneaking out again, aren't you?

980
01:53:45,714 --> 01:53:49,664
- Neville, listen. We were...
- No, I won't let you!

981
01:53:49,926 --> 01:53:54,505
You'll get Gryffindor into trouble again.
I'll fight you.

982
01:53:54,724 --> 01:53:59,018
<i>Neville, I'm really sorry about this.
Petrificus Totalus.</i>

983
01:54:06,985 --> 01:54:10,769
You're a little scary sometimes,
you know that?

984
01:54:11,031 --> 01:54:14,649
Brilliant, but scary.

985
01:54:15,327 --> 01:54:17,366
Let's go.

986
01:54:17,579 --> 01:54:21,826
- Sorry.
- It's for your own good, you know.

987
01:54:27,255 --> 01:54:31,205
- You stood on my foot!
- Sorry.

988
01:54:35,096 --> 01:54:37,136
<i>Alohomora.</i>

989
01:54:49,151 --> 01:54:51,725
Wait a minute. He's...

990
01:54:52,947 --> 01:54:55,105
...snoring.

991
01:54:57,618 --> 01:55:03,157
Snape's already been here.
He's put a spell on the harp.

992
01:55:04,749 --> 01:55:07,750
It's got horrible breath.

993
01:55:10,338 --> 01:55:12,415
- We have to move its paw.
- What?

994
01:55:12,633 --> 01:55:14,044
Come on!

995
01:55:18,098 --> 01:55:20,173
Okay. Push.

996
01:55:43,330 --> 01:55:46,949
I'll go first. Don't follow
until I give you a sign.

997
01:55:47,168 --> 01:55:52,162
If something bad happens,
get yourselves out.

998
01:55:52,964 --> 01:55:56,416
Does it seem a bit quiet to you?

999
01:55:57,135 --> 01:55:58,962
The harp.

1000
01:55:59,637 --> 01:56:02,342
It's stopped playing.

1001
01:56:12,399 --> 01:56:13,514
Jump!

1002
01:56:27,706 --> 01:56:31,325
Lucky this plant thing's here, really.

1003
01:56:45,765 --> 01:56:48,849
Stop moving, both of you.
This is Devil's Snare.

1004
01:56:49,062 --> 01:56:52,762
You have to relax. If you don't,
it will only kill you faster.

1005
01:56:52,982 --> 01:56:57,976
Kill us faster?
Oh, now I can relax!

1006
01:57:00,239 --> 01:57:01,568
Hermione!

1007
01:57:02,158 --> 01:57:05,941
- Now what are we gonna do?
- Just relax!

1008
01:57:06,161 --> 01:57:10,657
- Hermione, where are you?
- Do what I say! Trust me.

1009
01:57:17,756 --> 01:57:21,089
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

1010
01:57:21,301 --> 01:57:24,337
- He's not relaxing, is he?
- Apparently not.

1011
01:57:24,554 --> 01:57:27,092
- We've gotta do something.
- What?

1012
01:57:27,306 --> 01:57:30,224
I remember reading something
in Herbology.

1013
01:57:31,102 --> 01:57:34,934
Devil's Snare, Devil's Snare.
It's deadly fun...

1014
01:57:35,148 --> 01:57:39,525
...but will sulk in the sun!
That's it! It hates sunlight.

1015
01:57:39,778 --> 01:57:41,817
<i>Lumus Solem.</i>

1016
01:57:49,912 --> 01:57:52,486
- Ron, you okay?
- Yeah.

1017
01:57:55,209 --> 01:57:57,664
Lucky we didn't panic.

1018
01:57:58,421 --> 01:58:01,920
Lucky Hermione pays attention
in Herbology.

1019
01:58:03,550 --> 01:58:05,044
What is that?

1020
01:58:05,261 --> 01:58:08,961
I don't know. Sounds like wings.

1021
01:58:22,112 --> 01:58:25,563
Curious. I've never seen
birds like these.

1022
01:58:25,782 --> 01:58:29,400
They're not birds.
They're keys.

1023
01:58:29,619 --> 01:58:33,069
And I'll bet one of them
fits that door.

1024
01:58:36,542 --> 01:58:41,168
- What's this all about?
- I don't know.

1025
01:58:47,053 --> 01:58:49,092
Strange.

1026
01:58:49,513 --> 01:58:51,802
<i>Alohomora!</i>

1027
01:58:54,769 --> 01:58:57,010
Well, it was worth a try.

1028
01:58:57,229 --> 01:59:00,479
What will we do?
There must be a thousand keys.

1029
01:59:00,691 --> 01:59:04,604
We want a big, old-fashioned one.
Probably rusty.

1030
01:59:04,819 --> 01:59:08,235
I see it!
The one with the broken wing.

1031
01:59:11,826 --> 01:59:14,151
What's wrong?

1032
01:59:15,037 --> 01:59:16,531
It's too simple.

1033
01:59:16,747 --> 01:59:21,493
Go on! If Snape could catch it
on that old broomstick, you can.

1034
01:59:21,711 --> 01:59:25,246
You're the youngest Seeker
in a century.

1035
01:59:42,106 --> 01:59:45,106
This complicates things a bit.

1036
02:00:06,381 --> 02:00:08,290
Catch the key!

1037
02:00:12,720 --> 02:00:14,630
Hurry up!

1038
02:00:47,129 --> 02:00:51,790
I don't like this.
I don't like this at all.

1039
02:00:52,008 --> 02:00:55,175
Where are we? A graveyard.

1040
02:00:55,553 --> 02:00:58,174
This is no graveyard.

1041
02:01:05,687 --> 02:01:08,605
It's a chessboard.

1042
02:01:20,579 --> 02:01:22,488
There's the door.

1043
02:01:34,550 --> 02:01:36,045
Now what do we do?

1044
02:01:36,427 --> 02:01:40,555
It's obvious, isn't it? We've got
to play our way across the room.

1045
02:01:41,140 --> 02:01:44,888
Harry, you take
the empty bishop's square.

1046
02:01:45,228 --> 02:01:49,439
Hermione, you'll be
the queen-side castle.

1047
02:01:49,691 --> 02:01:53,735
As for me, I'll be a knight.

1048
02:02:00,909 --> 02:02:02,618
What happens now?

1049
02:02:03,412 --> 02:02:06,412
Well, white moves first.

1050
02:02:06,624 --> 02:02:08,497
And then...

1051
02:02:10,252 --> 02:02:11,497
...we play.

1052
02:02:22,098 --> 02:02:27,139
Ron, you don't suppose
this is going to be like...

1053
02:02:27,394 --> 02:02:30,929
...real wizard's chess, do you?

1054
02:02:31,315 --> 02:02:34,268
You there, d5.

1055
02:02:48,873 --> 02:02:50,451
Yes, Hermione.

1056
02:02:50,667 --> 02:02:55,743
I think this is gonna be
exactly like wizard's chess.

1057
02:03:01,679 --> 02:03:04,170
Castle to e4!

1058
02:03:07,809 --> 02:03:10,098
Pawn to c3!

1059
02:03:54,730 --> 02:03:58,727
- Wait a minute.
- You understand right, Harry.

1060
02:03:58,984 --> 02:04:03,692
Once I make my move,
the queen will take me.

1061
02:04:04,322 --> 02:04:06,647
Then you're free to check the king.

1062
02:04:06,866 --> 02:04:09,570
- No. Ron, no!
- What is it?

1063
02:04:10,204 --> 02:04:14,865
- He's going to sacrifice himself.
- No, there must be another way!

1064
02:04:15,083 --> 02:04:18,831
Do you wanna stop Snape
from getting that Stone or not?

1065
02:04:19,046 --> 02:04:22,629
Harry, it's you that has to go on.
I know it.

1066
02:04:23,134 --> 02:04:25,885
Not me. Not Hermione. You.

1067
02:04:36,145 --> 02:04:39,063
Knight to h3.

1068
02:05:00,002 --> 02:05:01,995
Check.

1069
02:05:31,158 --> 02:05:32,949
Ron!

1070
02:05:33,160 --> 02:05:38,949
No, don't move!
Don't forget, we're still playing.

1071
02:05:54,014 --> 02:05:55,294
Checkmate.

1072
02:06:15,244 --> 02:06:17,734
Take care of Ron.
Then go to the owlery.

1073
02:06:17,954 --> 02:06:21,821
Send a message to Dumbledore.
Ron's right.

1074
02:06:22,041 --> 02:06:23,914
I have to go on.

1075
02:06:24,418 --> 02:06:30,338
You'll be okay, Harry.
You're a great wizard. You really are.

1076
02:06:30,549 --> 02:06:33,040
Not as good as you.

1077
02:06:33,886 --> 02:06:38,714
Me? Books and cleverness.
There are more important things.

1078
02:06:39,934 --> 02:06:45,558
Friendship and bravery.
And, Harry, just be careful.

1079
02:07:23,644 --> 02:07:25,304
You?

1080
02:07:26,105 --> 02:07:29,937
No, it can't be.
Snape, he was the...

1081
02:07:30,150 --> 02:07:33,186
Yes, he does seem the type,
doesn't he?

1082
02:07:33,403 --> 02:07:36,523
Next to him, who would suspect...

1083
02:07:36,740 --> 02:07:40,654
...poor, stuttering
Professor Quirrell?

1084
02:07:40,869 --> 02:07:46,243
But that day, during the Quidditch match,
Snape tried to kill me.

1085
02:07:46,457 --> 02:07:49,245
No, dear boy. I tried to kill you!

1086
02:07:49,753 --> 02:07:53,917
If Snape's cloak hadn't caught
fire and broken my eye contact...

1087
02:07:54,132 --> 02:07:56,338
...I would have succeeded.

1088
02:07:56,551 --> 02:07:59,552
Even with Snape muttering
his countercurse.

1089
02:07:59,762 --> 02:08:01,969
Snape was trying to save me?

1090
02:08:02,182 --> 02:08:07,520
I knew you were a danger to me,
especially after Halloween.

1091
02:08:07,729 --> 02:08:11,975
- Then you let the troll in!
- Very good, Potter, yes.

1092
02:08:12,191 --> 02:08:15,191
Snape, unfortunately, wasn't fooled.

1093
02:08:15,778 --> 02:08:20,736
While everyone ran about,
he went to the third floor to head me off.

1094
02:08:21,659 --> 02:08:25,158
He, of course, never trusted me again.

1095
02:08:26,164 --> 02:08:31,406
He rarely left me alone.
But he doesn't understand.

1096
02:08:31,627 --> 02:08:35,671
I'm never alone. Never.

1097
02:08:35,882 --> 02:08:39,961
Now, what does this mirror do?

1098
02:08:41,553 --> 02:08:43,676
I see what I desire.

1099
02:08:44,222 --> 02:08:48,635
I see myself holding the Stone.
But how do I get it?

1100
02:08:48,852 --> 02:08:51,010
Use the boy.

1101
02:08:51,814 --> 02:08:55,728
Come here, Potter! Now!

1102
02:09:07,830 --> 02:09:11,828
Tell me, what do you see?

1103
02:09:36,984 --> 02:09:39,391
What is it? What do you see?

1104
02:09:39,611 --> 02:09:44,771
I'm shaking hands with Dumbledore.
I've won the house cup.

1105
02:09:44,991 --> 02:09:46,534
He lies.

1106
02:09:47,035 --> 02:09:50,735
Tell the truth! What do you see?

1107
02:09:50,955 --> 02:09:55,332
- Let me speak to him.
- Master, you are not strong enough.

1108
02:09:55,584 --> 02:09:59,582
I have strength enough for this.

1109
02:10:17,773 --> 02:10:20,644
Harry Potter...

1110
02:10:20,859 --> 02:10:23,184
...we meet again.

1111
02:10:23,404 --> 02:10:24,815
Voldemort.

1112
02:10:25,031 --> 02:10:28,981
Yes. You see what I've become?

1113
02:10:29,243 --> 02:10:32,825
See what I must do to survive?

1114
02:10:33,039 --> 02:10:37,166
Live off another. A mere parasite.

1115
02:10:37,835 --> 02:10:41,168
Unicorn blood can sustain me...

1116
02:10:41,379 --> 02:10:45,044
...but it cannot give me
a body of my own.

1117
02:10:45,258 --> 02:10:48,793
But there is something that can.

1118
02:10:49,013 --> 02:10:54,683
Something that, conveniently enough,
lies in your pocket.

1119
02:10:55,061 --> 02:10:56,602
Stop him!

1120
02:11:01,650 --> 02:11:04,401
Don't be a fool.

1121
02:11:04,903 --> 02:11:08,022
Why suffer an horrific death...

1122
02:11:08,239 --> 02:11:11,857
...when you can join me and live?

1123
02:11:12,076 --> 02:11:13,156
Never!

1124
02:11:15,163 --> 02:11:19,954
Bravery. Your parents had it too.

1125
02:11:20,710 --> 02:11:23,995
Tell me, Harry...

1126
02:11:24,255 --> 02:11:28,122
...would you like to see
your mother and father again?

1127
02:11:28,384 --> 02:11:30,461
Together...

1128
02:11:30,678 --> 02:11:33,216
...we can bring them back.

1129
02:11:33,640 --> 02:11:38,348
All I ask is for something in return.

1130
02:11:45,067 --> 02:11:48,187
That's it, Harry.

1131
02:11:49,071 --> 02:11:52,938
There is no good and evil.

1132
02:11:53,159 --> 02:11:56,160
There is only power...

1133
02:11:56,370 --> 02:12:00,498
...and those too weak to seek it.

1134
02:12:01,168 --> 02:12:06,209
Together, we'll do
extraordinary things.

1135
02:12:06,631 --> 02:12:08,873
Just give me the Stone!

1136
02:12:11,510 --> 02:12:12,673
You liar!

1137
02:12:12,886 --> 02:12:15,010
Kill him!

1138
02:12:38,537 --> 02:12:43,875
- What is this magic?
- Fool, get the Stone!

1139
02:14:29,145 --> 02:14:31,636
Good afternoon, Harry.

1140
02:14:33,775 --> 02:14:38,271
- Tokens from your admirers?
- Admirers?

1141
02:14:38,488 --> 02:14:44,491
What happened in the dungeons between
you and Professor Quirrell is a secret.

1142
02:14:44,702 --> 02:14:49,494
So, naturally, the whole school knows.

1143
02:14:51,833 --> 02:14:55,452
I see that your friend Ronald
has saved you the trouble...

1144
02:14:55,671 --> 02:14:58,506
...of opening your Chocolate Frogs.

1145
02:14:58,716 --> 02:15:01,717
Ron was here? Is he all right?
What about Hermione?

1146
02:15:01,929 --> 02:15:06,804
Fine. They're both just fine.

1147
02:15:07,392 --> 02:15:10,179
- What happened to the Stone?
- Relax, dear boy.

1148
02:15:10,520 --> 02:15:13,355
The Stone has been destroyed.

1149
02:15:13,606 --> 02:15:17,817
My friend Nicholas and I
have had a little chat...

1150
02:15:18,027 --> 02:15:21,976
...and agreed it was best all around.

1151
02:15:22,197 --> 02:15:26,029
But then, Flamel,
he'll die, won't he?

1152
02:15:28,078 --> 02:15:33,582
He has enough Elixir
to set his affairs in order.

1153
02:15:33,792 --> 02:15:36,995
But yes, he will die.

1154
02:15:37,212 --> 02:15:39,668
How is it I got the Stone, sir?

1155
02:15:39,883 --> 02:15:42,420
One minute I was staring
in the mirror and...

1156
02:15:42,635 --> 02:15:46,715
You see, only a person...

1157
02:15:47,014 --> 02:15:50,928
...who wanted to find the Stone,
find it...

1158
02:15:51,185 --> 02:15:55,727
...but not use it,
would be able to get it.

1159
02:15:56,690 --> 02:16:00,189
That is one of my more brilliant ideas.

1160
02:16:00,402 --> 02:16:05,443
And between you and me,
that is saying something.

1161
02:16:06,908 --> 02:16:12,115
Does that mean, with the Stone gone,
that Voldemort can never come back?

1162
02:16:12,330 --> 02:16:14,655
I'm afraid...

1163
02:16:16,084 --> 02:16:20,128
...there are ways
in which he can return.

1164
02:16:20,839 --> 02:16:23,411
Harry, do you know why...

1165
02:16:23,633 --> 02:16:27,631
...Professor Quirrell couldn't bear
to have you touch him?

1166
02:16:27,846 --> 02:16:32,472
It was because of your mother.
She sacrificed herself for you.

1167
02:16:33,017 --> 02:16:36,221
And that kind of act leaves a mark.

1168
02:16:36,438 --> 02:16:40,221
No, this kind of mark cannot be seen.

1169
02:16:40,441 --> 02:16:45,352
- It lives in your very skin.
- What is it?

1170
02:16:46,197 --> 02:16:49,945
Love, Harry. Love.

1171
02:16:58,001 --> 02:17:02,129
Bertie Bott's Every Flavor Beans.

1172
02:17:02,338 --> 02:17:07,000
I was most unfortunate in my youth
to come across a vomit-flavored one.

1173
02:17:07,259 --> 02:17:10,545
And since then,
I've lost my liking for them.

1174
02:17:10,763 --> 02:17:14,131
But I think I could be safe...

1175
02:17:14,349 --> 02:17:16,722
...with a nice toffee.

1176
02:17:20,814 --> 02:17:22,356
Alas!

1177
02:17:23,066 --> 02:17:25,189
Earwax.

1178
02:17:40,417 --> 02:17:43,584
- All right there, Ron?
- All right. You?

1179
02:17:44,712 --> 02:17:47,417
All right. Hermione?

1180
02:17:48,091 --> 02:17:49,918
Never better.

1181
02:18:05,735 --> 02:18:08,189
Another year gone.

1182
02:18:08,946 --> 02:18:13,489
And now, as I understand it,
the house cup needs awarding.

1183
02:18:13,700 --> 02:18:16,322
And the points stand thus:

1184
02:18:16,536 --> 02:18:22,325
In fourth place,
Gryffindor with 312 points.

1185
02:18:24,293 --> 02:18:29,963
Third place,
Hufflepuff with 352 points.

1186
02:18:35,263 --> 02:18:37,053
In second place...

1187
02:18:37,264 --> 02:18:42,056
...Ravenclaw with 426 points.

1188
02:18:47,734 --> 02:18:49,441
And in first place...

1189
02:18:49,777 --> 02:18:55,197
...with 472 points, Slytherin house.

1190
02:19:00,788 --> 02:19:02,994
Nice one, mate.

1191
02:19:06,835 --> 02:19:10,915
Yes, well done, Slytherin.
Well done.

1192
02:19:11,172 --> 02:19:15,466
However, recent events must
be taken into account.

1193
02:19:15,677 --> 02:19:20,635
And I have a few last-minute points
to award.

1194
02:19:21,266 --> 02:19:26,770
To Miss Hermione Granger,
for the cool use of intellect...

1195
02:19:26,981 --> 02:19:29,767
...while others were in grave peril...

1196
02:19:30,485 --> 02:19:32,726
...50 points.

1197
02:19:33,653 --> 02:19:34,934
Good job.

1198
02:19:42,662 --> 02:19:48,700
Second, to Mr. Ronald Weasley,
for the best-played game of chess...

1199
02:19:49,210 --> 02:19:54,453
...that Hogwarts has seen
these many years, 50 points.

1200
02:19:59,095 --> 02:20:01,135
And third...

1201
02:20:01,681 --> 02:20:04,552
...to Mr. Harry Potter...

1202
02:20:04,768 --> 02:20:09,061
...for pure nerve
and outstanding courage...

1203
02:20:09,647 --> 02:20:14,523
...I award Gryffindor house 60 points.

1204
02:20:22,826 --> 02:20:24,735
We're tied with Slytherin!

1205
02:20:24,953 --> 02:20:30,956
Finally, it takes a great deal of bravery
to stand up to your enemies...

1206
02:20:31,168 --> 02:20:35,035
...but a great deal more
to stand up to your friends.

1207
02:20:35,255 --> 02:20:38,209
I award 10 points...

1208
02:20:38,425 --> 02:20:41,629
...to Neville Longbottom.

1209
02:20:54,984 --> 02:20:58,399
Assuming that my calculations
are correct...

1210
02:20:58,612 --> 02:21:03,155
...I believe that a change
of decoration is in order.

1211
02:21:08,206 --> 02:21:11,574
Gryffindor wins the house cup.

1212
02:21:49,620 --> 02:21:52,954
Come on, now.
Hurry up, you'll be late.

1213
02:21:53,166 --> 02:21:57,459
Train's leaving. Go on.
Come on, hurry up.

1214
02:22:02,883 --> 02:22:06,168
- Come on, Harry.
- One minute.

1215
02:22:12,433 --> 02:22:16,182
Thought you were leaving
without saying goodbye, did you?

1216
02:22:19,400 --> 02:22:21,226
This is for you.

1217
02:22:38,002 --> 02:22:40,124
Thanks, Hagrid.

1218
02:22:45,967 --> 02:22:50,380
Go on. On with you. On with you now.
Oh, listen, Harry.

1219
02:22:50,805 --> 02:22:55,266
If that dolt of a cousin of yours,
Dudley, gives you any grief...

1220
02:22:55,519 --> 02:22:58,188
...you could always threaten him...

1221
02:22:58,397 --> 02:23:01,267
...with a nice pair of ears
to go with his tail.

1222
02:23:01,484 --> 02:23:06,560
But we're not allowed to do magic
away from Hogwarts. You know that.

1223
02:23:07,030 --> 02:23:11,360
I do. But your cousin don't, do he?

1224
02:23:16,872 --> 02:23:19,992
Feels strange to be going home,
doesn't it?

1225
02:23:20,209 --> 02:23:22,285
I'm not going home.

1226
02:23:22,503 --> 02:23:24,412
Not really.

